\'b2 The theme of the Binder-God and the magic knot has been the object of global mythological studies: notably Mircea Eliade, \ul \strokec2 Images et symboles\ulnone \strokec2 , Gallimard, ch. III. But these studies are ambiguous, because they use a syncretic or archetypal method. Dum\'e9zil's method is on the contrary differential: the theme of capture or of the bond gathers diverse data only under a differential trait, precisely constituted by political sovereignty. On the opposition of these two methods, one will refer to Ortigues, \ul \strokec2 Le discours et le symbole\ulnone \strokec2 , Aubier. \cf3 \strokec3 (Fr: 2; Minn: endnote, absent from supplied chunk)\cf0 \strokec2 \
\'b3 Dum\'e9zil, \ul \strokec2 Mitra-Varuna\ulnone \strokec2 , pp. 113\'96114, 151, 202\'96203.\

