\f2 \cf2 \'b66 fr.530 umn.426
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 On ne peut pas toutefois donner \'e0 ce sch\'e9ma un sens causal ( et les auteurs invoqu\'e9s ne le font pas ). En premier lieu, la machine de guerre n'explique rien ; car ou bien elle est ext\'e9rieure \'e0 l'Etat, et dirig\'e9e contre lui ; ou bien elle lui appartient d\'e9j\'e0, encast\'e9e ou appropri\'e9e, et elle le suppose. Si elle intervient dans une \'e9volution de l'Etat, c'est donc n\'e9cessairement en conjonction avec d'autres facteurs internes. Et c'est ce qui appara\'eet en second lieu : s'il y a une \'e9volution de l'Etat, il faut bien que le second p\'f4le, le p\'f4le \'e9volu\'e9, soit en r\'e9sonance avec le pre7. Marcel Detienne, Les ma\'eetres de v\'e9rit\'e9 . . . ; et \'ab La phalange, probl\'e8mes et controverses \'bb (in Probl\'e8mes de la guerre en Gr\'e8ce ancienne, Mouton). Cf. aussi J.-P. Vernant, Les origines de la pens\'e9e grecque. 53 1 mier, qu'il ne cesse de le recharger d'une certaine mani\'e8re, et que l'Etat n'ait qu'un seul milieu d'int\'e9riorit\'e9, c'est-\'e0-dire une unit\'e9 de composition) malgr\'e9 toutes les diff\'e9rences d'organisation et de d\'e9veloppement des Etats. Il faut m\'eame que chaque Etat ait les deux p\'f4les, comme les moments essentiels de son existence, bien que l'organisation des deux varie. En troisi\'e8me lieu, si l'on appelle \'ab capture \'bb cette essence int\'e9rieure ou cette unit\'e9 de l'Etat, nous devons dire que les mots de \'ab capture magique \'bb d\'e9crivent bien la situation, puisqu'elle appara\'eet toujours comme d\'e9j\'e0 faite et se pr\'e9supposant ; mais comment l'expliquer d\'e8s lors, si elle ne se rapporte \'e0 aucune cause assignable distincte ? C'est pourquoi les th\'e8ses sur l'origine de l'Etat sont toujours tautologiques.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 We cannot, however, assign this schema a causal meaning (the authors cited do not do SO). In the first place, the war machine explains nothing; for it is either exterior to the State, and directed against it; or else it already belongs to the State, encasted and appropriated, and presupposes it. If the war machine has a part in the evolution of the State, it is therefore necessarily in conjunction with other internal factors. And this is the second point: if there is an evolution of the State, the second pole, the evolved pole, must be in resonance with the first, it must continually recharge it in some way, and the State must have only one milieu of interiority; in other words, it must have a unity of composition, in spite of all the differences in organization and development among States. It is even necessary for each State to have both poles, as the essential moments of its existence, even though the organization of the two varies. Third, if we call this interior essence or this unity of the State "capture," we must say that the words "magic capture" describe the situation well because it always appears as preaccomplished and self -presupposing; but how is this capture to be explained then, if it leads back to no distinct assignable cause? That is why theses on the origin of the State are always tautological.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 One cannot however give this schema a causal sense (and the authors 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 invoqu\'e9s
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [invoked \'97 the legal register: to invoke an authority, cite in one's support; the scholars summoned as one invokes precedent]\cf0 \strokec2  do not do so). In the first place, the war machine explains nothing; for either it is exterior to the State, and directed against it; or else it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 lui appartient d\'e9j\'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [already belongs to it \'97 appartenir: ownership language, the d\'e9j\'e0 chain in property form]\cf0 \strokec2 , encast\'e9e or appropriated, and it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 le suppose
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [supposes it \'97 the supposer chain opens: the war machine supposes the State, as property will suppose public property, money the tax (\'b67)]\cf0 \strokec2 . If it intervenes in an evolution of the State, it is therefore necessarily in conjunction with other internal factors. And that is what appears in the second place: if there is an evolution of the State, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il faut bien que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [it must indeed be that \'97 il faut bien: the concessive-necessity idiom, "there's no getting around it": necessity granted under protest]\cf0 \strokec2  the second pole, the evolved pole, be in resonance with the first, that it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne cesse de le recharger
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [does not cease to recharge it \'97 ne cesser de, the plateau's continuous-aspect formula (cf. \'b61 ne cessent pas, \'b63 ne cesse pas); recharger: electrical and reloading register, the archaic pole kept charged, never superseded]\cf0 \strokec2  in a certain manner, and that the State have only one milieu of interiority, that is to say a unity of composition, despite all the differences of organization and development among States. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Il faut m\'eame que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [it must even be that \'97 the necessity escalated: falloir twice, the argument proceeding by constraint, not observation]\cf0 \strokec2  each State have the two poles, as the essential moments of its existence, although the organization of the two varies. In the third place, if one calls \'ab capture \'bb this interior essence or this unity of the State, we must say that the words \'ab magic capture \'bb 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e9crivent bien la situation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [describe the situation well \'97 bien as concessive grant: the words do fit, precisely because the thing is inexplicable]\cf0 \strokec2 , since it always appears as 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e9j\'e0 faite et se pr\'e9supposant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [already done and presupposing itself \'97 the d\'e9j\'e0 chain meets the pre- chain of \'b64: accomplished fact that is its own prerequisite, the tautology stated in two idioms]\cf0 \strokec2 ; but how to explain it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e8s lors
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [from then on, that being so \'97 the temporal-logical hinge: once this is granted, explanation is foreclosed]\cf0 \strokec2 , if it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se rapporte \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [relates back to, refers to \'97 relation of reference, not a trail to be followed back]\cf0 \strokec2  no distinct assignable cause? That is why theses on the origin of the State are always tautological.\

\f5 \uc0\u8311 
