\f2 \cf2 Proposition XI " Ce qui est premier ?
\f1 \

\f2 Le premier p\'f4le de capture, on l'appellera imp\'e9rial ou despotique. Il correspond \'e0 la formation asiatique de Marx. L'arch\'e9ologie 8. Jacques Harmand (La guerre antique) P. U. F., p. 28) cite \'ab l'entre\'b7 prise \'e0 gros effectifs conduite singuli\'e8rement par un fonctionnaire civil, Ouni, wus le pharaon Pepi !('r vers 1400 \'bb . M\'eame la d\'e9mocratie militaire telle que Morgan la d\'e9crivait suppose un Etat archa\'efque de type imp\'e9rial, et ne l'explique pas (c'est ce qui r\'e9sulte des travaux de Detienne et de Vernant). Cet Etat imp\'e9rial lui-m\'eame proc\'e8de d'abord avec des ge\'f4liers et des policiers, plut\'f4t qu'avec des guerriers : cf. Dum\'e9zil, Mitra-Varuna) pp. 200-204. le d\'e9couvre partout, souvent recouvert par l'oubli, \'e0 l'horizon de tous les syst\'e8mes ou Etats, non seulement en Asie, mais en Afrique, en Am\'e9rique, en Gr\'e8ce, \'e0 Rome. Urstaat imm\'e9morial, d\'e8s le n\'e9olithique, et peut-\'eatre encore plus haut. Suivant la description marxiste : un appareil d'Etat s'\'e9rige sur les communaut\'e9s primitives agricoles, gui ont d\'e9j\'e0 des codes lignagers-territoriaux ; mais il les surcode, les soumet au pouvoir d'un empereur despote, propri\'e9taire public unique et transcendant, ma\'eetre du surplus ou du stock, organisateur des grands travaux ( surtravail), source de fonctions publiques et de bureaucratie. C'est le paradigme du lien, du n\'9cud. Tel est le r\'e9gime de signes de l'Etat : le surcodage ou le Signifiant. C'est un syst\'e8me d'asservissement machinique : la premi\'e8re \'ab m\'e9gamachine \'bb \'e0 proprement parler, comme dit Mumford. Prodigieuse r\'e9ussite en un coup : les autres Etats ne seront que des avortons par rapport \'e0 ce mod\'e8le. L'empereur-despote n'est pas un roi ou un tyran ; ceux-ci n'existeront qu'en fonction d'une propri\'e9t\'e9 d\'e9j\'e0 priv\'e9e 9. Tandis que tout est public dans le r\'e9gime imp\'e9rial : la possession de la terre y est communautaire, chacun ne poss\'e8de qu'en tant que membre d'une communaut\'e9 ; la propri\'e9t\'e9 \'e9minente du despote est celle de l'Unit\'e9 suppos\'e9e des communes ; et les fonctionnaires euxm\'eames n'ont que des terres de fonction, m\'eame h\'e9r\'e9ditaires. L'argent peut exister, notamment dans l'imp\'f4t que les fonctionnaires doivent \'e0 l'empereur, mais il sert pas \'e0 une vente-achat, puisque la terre n'existe pas comme marchandise ali\'e9nable.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 PROPOSITION XI. Which comes first?
\f1 \

\f2 We shall call the first pole of capture imperial or despotic. It corresponds to Marx's Asiatic formation. Archaeology discovers it everywhere, often lost in oblivion, at the horizon of all systems or States-not only in Asia, but also in Africa, America, Greece, Rome. Immemorial Urstaat, dating as far back as Neolithic times, and perhaps farther still. Following the Marxist description: a State apparatus is erected upon the primitive agricultural communities, which already have lineal-territorial codes; but it overcodes 428 0 7000 B.c.: APPARA TUS OF CAPTURE them, submitting them to the power of a despotic emperor, the sole and transcendent public-property owner, the master of the surplus or the stock, the organizer oflarge-scale works (surplus labor), the source of public functions and bureaucracy. This is the paradigm of the bond, the knot. Such is the regime of signs of the State: overcoding, or the Signifier. It is a system of machinic enslavement: the first "megamachine" in the strict sense, to use Mumf ord's term. A prodigious success in a single stroke; other States will be mere runts measured against this model. The emperor-despot is not a king or a tyrant; these will come into existence only as a function of private property once it has arisen.9 In the imperial regime, everything is public: ownership ofland is communal, each indi vidual is an owner only insofar as he or she is a member of the community; the eminent property of the despot is that of the supposed Unity of the communities; and the functionaries themselves have land only if it comes with their position (although the position may be hereditary). Money may exist, notably in the form of the tax that the functionaries owe the emperor, but it is not used for buyingselling, since land does not exist as an alienable commodity.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Proposition XI: 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce qui est premier ?
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [What is first? \'97 nominal: priority of essence, not sequence; not "which comes first"]\cf0 \strokec2 \
The first pole of capture, one will call it imperial or despotic. It corresponds to Marx's Asiatic formation. Archaeology discovers it everywhere, often 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 recouvert
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [covered over \'97 archaeological layering: buried under forgetting, not lost in it]\cf0 \strokec2  by forgetting, at the horizon of all systems or States, not only in Asia, but in Africa, in America, in Greece, at Rome. Immemorial Urstaat, from the Neolithic on, and perhaps from 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 encore plus haut
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [higher still \'97 the stratigrapher's vertical: earlier as higher up the dig, time measured in layers]\cf0 \strokec2 . Following the Marxist description: a State apparatus 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'\'e9rige sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [erects itself upon \'97 \'e9riger: the monument register, a thing raised; reflexive: self-raising, no builder named]\cf0 \strokec2  the primitive agricultural communities, which already have lineage-territorial codes; but it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 surcode
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [overcodes \'97 sur-, over: a coding laid on top of codes already there; the plateau's regime-of-signs term]\cf0 \strokec2  them, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 soumet au pouvoir
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [submits to the power \'97 soumettre: subjection as formal act, the vocabulary of vassalage]\cf0 \strokec2  of a despot emperor, unique and transcendent public proprietor, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ma\'eetre du surplus ou du stock
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [master of the surplus or the stock \'97 ma\'eetre de: title of ownership and command, the \'b65 Master of truth now master of grain]\cf0 \strokec2 , organizer of the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 grands travaux
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [great works \'97 the \'b61 set phrase returns: State public works, corv\'e9e register]\cf0 \strokec2  (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 surtravail
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [surplus labor \'97 Marx's Mehrarbeit; the same sur- as surcodage: labor over and above]\cf0 \strokec2 ), source of public 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fonctions
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  and of bureaucracy \cf3 \strokec3 [functions \'97 the fonction chain opens: fonctions publiques, fonctionnaires, terres de fonction, en fonction de \'97 office, official, office-land, and the mathematical "as a function of," one word through all four]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is the paradigm of the lien, of the knot. Such is the regime of signs of the State: surcodage, or the Signifier. It is a system of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 asservissement machinique
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [machinic enslavement \'97 asservir, to enslave; also the engineering register: to make into a servomechanism, slaved components]\cf0 \strokec2 : the first \'ab megamachine \'bb 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e0 proprement parler
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [properly speaking \'97 the parler idiom family (\'b62 parler trop vite): speech policing its own exactness]\cf0 \strokec2 , as Mumford says. Prodigious 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 r\'e9ussite en un coup
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [success at one stroke \'97 the coup chain: cf. the Urstaat surging d'un coup, \'b67]\cf0 \strokec2 : the other States will be only 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 avortons
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [runts, abortlings \'97 avorter, to abort: States as miscarriages of the model; the birth-frame of \'b67 continued \'97 born adult vs. born runt]\cf0 \strokec2  in relation to this model. The emperor-despot is not a king or a tyrant; those will exist only 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en fonction d'une propri\'e9t\'e9 d\'e9j\'e0 priv\'e9e
\f5\i0\b0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8313 
\f3  \cf3 \strokec3 [as a function of a property already private \'97 the fonction chain gone mathematical: king and tyrant as dependent variables of private property; d\'e9j\'e0 chain]\cf0 \strokec2 . Whereas everything is public in the imperial regime: possession of the land there is communal, each possesses only 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en tant que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  member of a community \cf3 \strokec3 [in the capacity of \'97 the title-formula family (au titre de, \'b616): possession by status, not person]\cf0 \strokec2 ; the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 propri\'e9t\'e9 \'e9minente
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [eminent property \'97 legal term of art: dominium eminens, the overlord's superior title above all holdings]\cf0 \strokec2  of the despot is that of the supposed Unity of the communes; and the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fonctionnaires
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  themselves have only 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 terres de fonction
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [function-lands \'97 lands attached to the office, prebendal tenure: the fonction chain in soil]\cf0 \strokec2 , even hereditary ones. Money can exist, notably in 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'imp\'f4t
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the tax \'97 the compte chain: the fiscal relation preceding commerce, developed at \'b69's rente]\cf0 \strokec2  that the functionaries owe the emperor, but it does not serve a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 vente-achat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [sale-purchase \'97 the hyphenated pair as one act: commerce as a single two-faced operation, not yet existing]\cf0 \strokec2 , since the land does not exist as alienable merchandise.\

\f5 \uc0\u8312 
\f3  Jacques Harmand (\ul \strokec2 La guerre antique\ulnone \strokec2 , P.U.F., p. 28) cites \'ab the large-scale enterprise conducted singularly by a civil functionary, Uni, under the pharaoh Pepi I, around 1400 \'bb. \cf3 \strokec3 [Harmand is French-original: translated from the supplied French. Date flag stands: "vers 1400" almost certainly OCR or edition error \'97 Uni served Pepi I, c. 2300 B.C.; check print Minuit for \'ab vers 2400 \'bb; if print reads 1400, preserve with sic]\cf0 \strokec2  Even military democracy as Morgan described it supposes an archaic State of imperial type, and does not explain it (this is what results from the works of D\'e9tienne and Vernant). This imperial State itself proceeds at first with jailers and policemen, rather than with warriors: cf. Dum\'e9zil, \ul \strokec2 Mitra-Varuna\ulnone \strokec2 , pp. 200\'96204. \cf3 \strokec3 (text for \'b67's marker, delivered here)\cf0 \strokec2 \
