\f2 \cf2 C'est le r\'e9gime du nexum, le lien : quelque chose est pr\'eat\'e9 ou m\'eame donn\'e9 sans transfert de propri\'e9t\'e9, sans appropriation priv\'e9e, et dont la contrepartie ne pr\'e9sente pas un int\'e9r\'eat ni un profit pour le donateur, mais plut\'f4t une \'ab rente \'bb qui lui revient, accompagnant le pr\'eat d'usage ou la donation de revenu 10 . 9. L'id\'e9e m\'eame d'une formation despotique asiatique appara\'eet au xvnre si\'e8cle, notamment chez Montesquieu, mais pour d\'e9crire un \'e9tat \'e9volu\'e9 des empires, et en rorrespondance avec la monarchie absolue. Tout autre est le point de vue de Marx, qui recr\'e9e la notion pour d\'e9finir les empires archa\'efques. Les textes principaux \'e0 cet \'e9gard sont : Marx, Grundrisse, Pl\'e9iade II, pp. 312 sq. ; Wittfogel, Le despotisme oriental, Ed. de Minuit (et l'avant-propos de Vidal-Naquet dans la premi\'e8re \'e9dition, mais qui fut supprim\'e9 dans la seconde \'e0 la demande de Wittfogel) ; Tokei, Sur le mode de production asiatique, Studia historica 1966 ; l'\'e9tude d'ensemble du C. E. R. M., Sur le mode de production asiatique\} Ed. Sociales. 10. Varron faisait un jeu de mots c\'e9l\'e8bre entre nexum et nec suum fit ( = la chose ne devient pas la propri\'e9t\'e9 de celui qui la re\'e7oit). En effet, le nexttm est une forme fondamentale du droit romain archa\'efque, o\'f9 ce qui oblige n'est pas un accord entre parties contractantes, mais uniquement la parole du pr\'eateur ou du donateur, sur un mode magico-religieux.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 This is the regime of the nexum, the bond: something is lent or even given without a transfer of ownership, without private appropriation, and the compensation for it does not come in the form of interest or profit for the donor but rather as a "rent" that accrues to him, accompanying the lending of something for another's use or the granting of revenue. 1 0
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It is the regime of the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 nexum
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [nexum \'97 archaic Roman-law bond of the debtor; Latin nectere, to bind: the lien/knot chain in juridical form]\cf0 \strokec2 , the lien: something is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pr\'eat\'e9 ou m\'eame donn\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [lent or even given \'97 the pr\'eater/donner pair: two grades of one gesture, both without alienation; the pair returns below as pr\'eat d'usage / donation de revenu, lender / donor]\cf0 \strokec2  without transfer of property, without private appropriation, and whose 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 contrepartie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [counterpart, counter-performance \'97 the bookkeeper's contrepartie, the balancing entry on the other side of the ledger: the compte chain, not "compensation" for a loss]\cf0 \strokec2  presents neither an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 int\'e9r\'eat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  nor a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 profit
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  for the donor \cf3 \strokec3 [interest nor profit \'97 the two commercial returns named to be excluded: the fiscal relation defined by subtraction, no usury, no margin]\cf0 \strokec2 , but rather a \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rente
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb \cf3 \strokec3 [rent \'97 the economic term of art: return owed without sale, interest, or profit; ground-rent register, a keyword of this plateau]\cf0 \strokec2  that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 lui revient
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [comes back to him \'97 revenir: what returns by right, the idiom of rightful accrual (cela lui revient, "that is his due"); sounding revenu, revenue: the return that returns as income]\cf0 \strokec2 , accompanying the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pr\'eat d'usage
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [loan for use \'97 commodatum: the use is lent, the thing is not alienated; usage, the usufruct register of \'b65's jouit]\cf0 \strokec2  or the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 donation de revenu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 \'b9
\f5 \uc0\u8304 
\f3  \cf3 \strokec3 [donation of revenue \'97 the gift whose content is income itself: giving the flow, keeping the source]\cf0 \strokec2 .\

\f5 \uc0\u8313 
\f3  The very idea of an Asiatic despotic formation appears in the eighteenth century, notably in Montesquieu, but to describe an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9tat \'e9volu\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the empires \cf3 \strokec3 [evolved state \'97 \'e9tat, lowercase: condition, stage; the same word as \'c9tat hovering under it \'97 a "state of the empires" that is not yet the State]\cf0 \strokec2 , and in correspondence with absolute monarchy. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Tout autre est le point de vue de Marx
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [entirely other is Marx's point of view \'97 inverted attack, predicate first: the treatise's gesture of turning on its heel]\cf0 \strokec2 , who recreates the notion to define the archaic empires. The principal texts in this regard are: Marx, \ul \strokec2 Grundrisse\ulnone \strokec2 , Pl\'e9iade II, pp. 312 ff.; Wittfogel, \ul \strokec2 Le despotisme oriental\ulnone \strokec2 , \'c9d. de Minuit (and the foreword by Vidal-Naquet in the first edition, but which was suppressed in the second at Wittfogel's request); Tokei, \ul \strokec2 Sur le mode de production asiatique\ulnone \strokec2 , Studia historica 1966; the collective study of the C.E.R.M., \ul \strokec2 Sur le mode de production asiatique\ulnone \strokec2 , \'c9d. Sociales. \cf3 \strokec3 [Marx flag closed as bibliographic \'97 no wording to verify]\cf0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 (text for \'b68's marker, delivered here)\cf0 \strokec2 \
\'b9
\f5 \uc0\u8304 
\f3  Varro made a famous 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 jeu de mots
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [play on words \'97 D&G naming wordplay as such: the pun as juridical evidence]\cf0 \strokec2  between nexum and nec suum fit (= the thing does not become the property of the one who receives it). Indeed, the nexum is a fundamental form of archaic Roman law, where 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ce qui oblige
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [what obliges \'97 obliger: the root of obligation, ob-ligare, to bind toward: the lien chain hiding inside legal "obligation" itself]\cf0 \strokec2  is not an accord between contracting 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 parties
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , but solely 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 la parole
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the lender or of the donor \cf3 \strokec3 [the word \'97 parole: the spoken word as binding force, the magico-religious speech-act; the same parole that \'b613 will make presuppose the State]\cf0 \strokec2 , on a magico-religious mode.\
