\f2 \cf2 \'b610 fr.532 umn.428
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Ce n'est pas un contrat (mancipatio), et il ne comporte ni vente-achat, m\'eame diff\'e9r\'e9, ni int\'e9r\'eat, bien qu'il puisse, nous semble-t-il, comporter une Marx historien, Childe arch\'e9ologue, s'accordent sur le point suivant : l'Etat imp\'e9rial archa\'efque, qui vient surcoder des communaut\'e9s agricoles, suppose au moins un certain d\'e9veloppement de leurs forces productives, puisqu'il faut un surplus potentiel capable de constituer le stock d'Etat, d'entretenir un artisanat sp\'e9cialis\'e9 (m\'e9tallurgie), et de susciter progressivement des fonctions publiques. Ce pourquoi Marx liait l'Etat archa\'efque \'e0 un certain < mode de production \'bb . Toutefois, on n'a pas fini de reculer dans le temps l'origine de ces Etats n\'e9olithiques. Or, quand on conjecture des empires presque pal\'e9olithiques, il ne s'agit pas seulement d'une quantit\'e9 de temps, c'est le probl\'e8me qualitatif qui change. \'c7atal-H\'fcy\'fck, en Anatolie, rend possible un paradigme imp\'e9rial singuli\'e8rement renforc\'e9 : c'est un stock de graines sauvages et d'animaux relativement paisibles, issus de territoires diff\'e9rents, qui op\'e8re et permet d'op\'e9rer, d'abord au hasard, des hybridations et des s\'e9lections d'o\'f9 l'agriculture et le petit \'e9levage sortiront 1 1 . On voit l'importance de ce changement dans les donn\'e9es du probl\'e8me. Ce n'est plus le stock qui suppose un surplus potentiel, mais l'inverse. Ce n'est plus l'Etat qui suppose des communaut\'e9s agricoles \'e9labor\'e9es, et des forces productives d\'e9velopp\'e9es ; au contraire, il s'\'e9tablit directement dans un milieu de cueilleurs-chasseurs sans agriculture ni m\'e9tallurgie pr\'e9alables, et c'est lui qui cr\'e9e l'agriculture, l'\'e9levage et la m\'e9tallurgie, d'abord sur son propre sol, puis les impose au monde environnant. Ce n'est plus la campagne qui cr\'e9e progressivement la ville, c'est la ville qui cr\'e9e la campagne.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Marx, the historian, and Childe, the archaeologist, are in agreement on the following point: the archaic imperial State, which steps in to overcode agricultural communities, presupposes at least a certain level of development of these communities' productive forces since there must be a potential surplus capable of constituting a State stock, of supporting a specialized handicrafts class (metallurgy), and of progressively giving rise to public functions. That is why Marx links the archaic State to a certain "mode of production." However, the origin of these Neolithic States is still being pushed back in time. What is at issue when the existence of nearPaleolithic empires is conjectured is not simply the quantity of time; the qualitative problem changes. (atal Htiytik, in Anatolia, makes possible a singularly reinforced imperial paradigm: it is a stock of uncultivated seeds and relatively tame animals from diff erent territories that perf orms, and makes it possible to perform, at first by chance, hybridizations and selections from which agriculture and small-scale animal raising arise. I I It is easy to see the significance of this change in the givens of the problem. It is no longer the stock that presupposes a potential surplus, but the other way around. It is no longer the State that presupposes advanced agricultural communities and developed forces of production. On the contrary, the State is established directly in a milieu of hunter-gatherers having no prior 7000 B.C.: APPARATUS OF CAPTURE 0 429 agriculture or metallurgy, and it is the State that creates agriculture, animal raising, and metallurgy; it does so first on its own soil, then imposes them upon the surrounding world. It is not the country that progressively creates the town but the town that creates the country.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It is not a contract (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 mancipatio
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ) \cf3 \strokec3 [mancipatio \'97 Roman law: the formal conveyance by bronze and scales, transfer of ownership proper; named to mark exactly what the nexum is not]\cf0 \strokec2 , and it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 comporte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  neither 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 vente-achat, m\'eame diff\'e9r\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , nor interest \cf3 \strokec3 [comprises neither sale-purchase, even deferred \'97 the \'b68 pair again; diff\'e9r\'e9: the credit-sale, purchase postponed \'97 even commerce-on-delay is excluded]\cf0 \strokec2 , although it can, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 nous semble-t-il
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , comprise a\'85 \cf3 \strokec3 [it seems to us \'97 the authors' hedge, rare first-person plural: D&G marking their own conjecture inside a legal exposition]\cf0 \strokec2  \
Marx the historian, Childe the archaeologist, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'accordent sur le point suivant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [accord themselves on the following point \'97 s'accorder: the treaty-word, parties reaching accord (\'b69 fn.: accord entre parties); historian and archaeologist as contracting parties]\cf0 \strokec2 : the archaic imperial State, which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 vient surcoder
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [comes to overcode \'97 venir + infinitive: the State arrives upon communities already there, overcoding as intervention from outside]\cf0 \strokec2  agricultural communities, supposes at least a certain development of their productive forces, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 puisqu'il faut
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [since there must be \'97 falloir again (\'b66): the argument by necessity, here granted to the adversary's case]\cf0 \strokec2  a potential surplus capable of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 constituer le stock d'\'c9tat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [constituting the State stock \'97 stock: the granary register, the despot's mastered reserve (\'b68 ma\'eetre du stock)]\cf0 \strokec2 , of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 entretenir
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  a specialized artisanry \cf3 \strokec3 [maintaining \'97 entretenir: to keep up, keep fed: the State as household head provisioning its crafts]\cf0 \strokec2  (metallurgy), and of progressively 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 susciter
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  public functions \cf3 \strokec3 [calling forth \'97 susciter: to raise up, summon into being; near-theological register, cf. s'\'e9riger \'b68]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce pourquoi
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [which is why \'97 clipped connective, drier than "c'est pourquoi": the treatise's shorthand]\cf0 \strokec2  Marx tied the archaic State to a certain \'ab mode of production \'bb. However, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 on n'a pas fini de reculer dans le temps
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one has not finished pushing back in time \'97 n'avoir pas fini de: the idiom of the still-unrolling process, "we haven't seen the end of it"; reculer: the origin retreating as the diggers advance]\cf0 \strokec2  the origin of these Neolithic States. Now, when one 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 conjecture
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  almost-Paleolithic empires \cf3 \strokec3 [conjectures \'97 the mathematician's verb: empires posited as conjecture, awaiting proof]\cf0 \strokec2 , 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il ne s'agit pas seulement de
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  a quantity of time \cf3 \strokec3 [it is not a matter only of \'97 s'agir de: the impersonal what-is-at-stake formula, tracked on-machinery]\cf0 \strokec2 , it is the qualitative problem that changes. \'c7atal H\'fcy\'fck, in Anatolia, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rend possible
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [renders possible \'97 the causative rendre: the site does not prove but enables the paradigm]\cf0 \strokec2  a singularly reinforced imperial paradigm: it is a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 stock
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of wild seeds and of relatively 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 paisibles
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  animals \cf3 \strokec3 [peaceable \'97 temperament, not domestication: not yet tame, merely tractable; the stock precedes the breeding]\cf0 \strokec2 , 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 issus de
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  different territories \cf3 \strokec3 [issuing from \'97 issu de: born of, descended from: the birth-frame again, seeds and beasts with territorial parentage]\cf0 \strokec2 , that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 op\'e8re et permet d'op\'e9rer, d'abord au hasard
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [operates and permits operating, at first by chance \'97 op\'e9rer, the \'b61 emperor's verb now the stock's own; au hasard: the aleatory, selection before any selector]\cf0 \strokec2 , hybridizations and selections from which agriculture and small 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9levage
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  will come out\'b9\'b9 \cf3 \strokec3 [stock-raising \'97 \'e9levage, from \'e9lever, to raise: rearing as elevation, the herd raised as the State s'\'e9rige]\cf0 \strokec2 . One sees the importance of this change in the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 donn\'e9es
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the problem \cf3 \strokec3 [givens \'97 the data of a problem, schoolbook register: what the problem statement supplies]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is no longer the stock that supposes a potential surplus, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'inverse
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the inverse \'97 the mathematical flip: the plateau's recurring operator (\'b611 twice), whole causal orders reversed in one word]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is no longer the State that supposes elaborated agricultural communities, and developed productive forces; on the contrary, it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'\'e9tablit directement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [establishes itself directly \'97 the reflexive again (s'\'e9rige \'b68): self-installing, no prior ground needed]\cf0 \strokec2  in a milieu of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 cueilleurs-chasseurs
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [gatherers-hunters \'97 French order: gathering first, the seed-stock not the hunt as the State's material]\cf0 \strokec2  without 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pr\'e9alables
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  agriculture or metallurgy \cf3 \strokec3 [prior \'97 pr\'e9alable: the pre- chain, prerequisite denied]\cf0 \strokec2 , and it is the State that creates agriculture, \'e9levage and metallurgy, at first 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 sur son propre sol
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [on its own soil \'97 the proprietary ground: the State experiments at home, then exports]\cf0 \strokec2 , then imposes them on the surrounding world. It is no longer the countryside that progressively creates the town, it is the town that creates the countryside.\
