\f2 \cf2 On n'en inf\'e9rera pas, cependant, une \'e9volution m\'eame en zigzag qui irait des primitifs aux Etats, des Etats aux machines de guerre nomades : ou du moins le zigzag n'est 13. Selon Gryaznov, ce sont des agriculteurs s\'e9dentaires qui se mettent \'e0 nomadiser dans la steppe, \'e0 l'\'e2ge du bronze : c'est le cas d'un mouvement en zigzag dans l'\'e9volution. Cf. Sib\'e9rie du Sud) Nagel, pp. 99, 133134. A P P A IW I L DE C A PTUR E pas successif, mais passe par les l ieux d'une topologie qui d\'e9finit ici des soci\'e9t\'e9s primitives , l\'e0 des Etats, l\'e0 des machines de guerre. Et m\'eame quand l'Etat s'approprie la machine de guerre, en en changeant encore la nature, c'est un ph\'e9nom\'e8ne de transport, de transfert, et non d'\'e9volution. Le nomade n'existe qu'en devenir, et en interaction ; mais le primitif aussi. L'histoire ne fait que traduire en succession une coexistence de devenirs. Et les collectivit\'e9s peuvent \'eatre transhumantes, semi-s\'e9dentaires, s\'e9dentaires ou nomades, sans \'eatre pour autant des stades pr\'e9paratoires de l'Etat, qui se trouve d\'e9j\'e0 l\'e0, ailleurs ou \'e0 c\'f4t\'e9.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 We cannot, however, inf er from this even a zigzag evolution that would go from primitive peoples to States, from States to nomad war machines; or at least the zigzagging is not successive but passes through the loci of a topology that defines primiti ve societies here, States there, and elsewhere war machines. And even when the State appropriates the war machine, once again changing its nature, it is a phenomenon of transport, of transfer, and not one of evolution. The nomad exists only in becoming, and in interaction; the same goes for the primitive. All history does is to translate a coexistence of becomings into a succession. And collectivities can be transhumant, 7000 B.c.: APPARA TUS OF CAPTURE 0 431 semisedentary, sedentary, or nomadic, without by the same token being preparatory stages for the State, which is already there, elsewhere or beside.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\i\b \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 On n'en inf\'e9rera pas, cependant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one will not infer from it, however \'97 the instruction-future + impersonal on (\'b62's on ne confondra pas): the treatise forbidding a conclusion]\cf0 \strokec2 , an evolution even in zigzag that would go from the primitives to States, from States to nomad war machines: or 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 du moins
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [at the least \'97 the fallback qualifier: conceding the zigzag to deny its sequence]\cf0 \strokec2  the zigzag is not successive, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 passe par les lieux d'une topologie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [passes by way of the places of a topology \'97 the routing idiom again (\'b613, \'b614): waypoints, not stages; lieux: positions in a space, the mathematician's loci]\cf0 \strokec2  that defines here primitive societies, there States, there machines de guerre. And even when the State 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'approprie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the war machine \cf3 \strokec3 [appropriates to itself \'97 the reflexive of taking-as-one's-own: property-verb, the capture in grammatical miniature]\cf0 \strokec2 , changing its nature yet again, it is a phenomenon of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 transport, de transfert
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [transport, transfer \'97 displacement across the topology: movement of place, not advance of stage; transfert also the legal transfer of title]\cf0 \strokec2 , and not of evolution. The nomad exists only in 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 devenir
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , and in interaction; but the primitive too. History 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne fait que traduire
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [does nothing but translate \'97 ne faire que: the restrictive, history's whole work reduced to one operation; traduire: the translation-chain of \'b613 \'97 history renders coexistence into the other idiom, succession; also the legal traduire, to hale before a court]\cf0 \strokec2  into succession a coexistence of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 devenirs
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . And the collectivities can be 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 transhumantes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [transhumant \'97 seasonal herding between fixed pastures: a fourth conduct beside \'b614's series]\cf0 \strokec2 , semi-sedentary, sedentary, or nomad, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 sans \'eatre pour autant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [without for all that being \'97 pour autant: the concession-blocker, "it does not follow"]\cf0 \strokec2  preparatory stages of the State, which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se trouve d\'e9j\'e0 l\'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [finds itself already there \'97 the reflexive + d\'e9j\'e0 chain: the State discovered in place, self-located, no arrival]\cf0 \strokec2 , elsewhere or 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e0 c\'f4t\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [beside, next door \'97 lateral position: alongside, never ahead on a line]\cf0 \strokec2 .\
\'b9\'b3 According to Gryaznov, it is sedentary agriculturalists who set about nomadizing in the steppe, at the Bronze Age: it is the case of a zigzag movement in evolution. Cf. \ul \strokec2 Sib\'e9rie du Sud\ulnone \strokec2 , Nagel, pp. 99, 133\'96134.\
