\f2 \cf2 \'b625 fr.541 umn.435
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Le probl\'e8me de la diffusion, du difEusionnisme, est mal pos\'e9 tant qu'on pr\'e9suppose un centre \'e0 partir duquel la diffusion se ferait. Il n'y a de diffusion que par mise en communication de potentiels d'ordre tr\'e8s diff\'e9rents raisons de la victoire des Etats sur les villes \'e0 partir du xve si\'e8cle, c'est que l'Etat seul a la facult\'e9 de s'approprier pleinement la machine de guerre : par recrutement territorial des hommes, investissement mat\'e9riel, industrialisation de la guerre (c'est dans les manufactures d'armes plus que dans les fabriques d'\'e9pingles que la production en s\'e9rie et la division m\'e9canique apparaissent) . Les villes commer\'e7antes au contraire ont besoin de guerres rapides, recourent \'e0 des mercenaires, et ne peuvent qu'encaster la machine de guerre. toute diffusion proc\'e8de au milieu, par le milieu, comme tout ce qui < pousse \'bb, du type rhizome. Une organisation internationale \'9ccum\'e9nique ne proc\'e8de pas d'un centre imp\'e9rial qui s'imposerait \'e0 un milieu ext\'e9rieur pour l'homog\'e9n\'e9iser ; elle ne se r\'e9duit pas davantage \'e0 des relations entre formations de m\'eame ordre, par exemple entre Etats ( S. D. N . , O . N. U . . . ) . Au contraire, elle constitue un milieu interm\'e9diaire entre les diff\'e9rents ordres coexistants. Aussi bien n'est-elle pas \'e9conomique ou commerciale exclusivement, elle est aussi bien religieuse, artistique, etc. C'est en ce sens qu'on appellera organisation internationale tout ce qui a l'aptitude de passer par des formations sociales diverses, simultan\'e9ment, Etats, villes, d\'e9serts, machines de guerre, soci\'e9t\'e9s primitives. Les grandes formations commer\'e7antes historiques n'ont pas simplement des cit\'e9s-p\'f4les, mais des segments primitifs, imp\'e9riaux, nomades, par lesquels elles passent, quitte \'e0 ressortir sous une autre forme.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 The problem of diff usion, or of diff usionism, is badly formulated if one assumes a center at which the diff usion would begin. Diff usion occurs only through the placing in communication of potentials of very different orders: all diffusion happens in the in-between, goes between, like everything that "grows" of the rhizome type. An international ecumenical organization does not proceed from an imperial center that imposes itself upon and homogenizes an exterior milieu; neither is it reducible to relations between formations of the same order, between States, for example (the League of Nations, the United Nations). On the contrary, it constitutes an intermediate milieu between the dif ferent coexistent orders. Therefore it is not exclusively commercial or economic, but is also religious, artistic, etc. From this standpoint, we shall call an international organization anything that has the capacity to move through diverse social formations simultaneously: States, towns, deserts, war machines, primitive societies. The great commercial formations in history do not simply have city-poles, but also primitive, imperial, and nomadic segments through which they pass, perhaps issuing out again in another form.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'b9
\f5 \uc0\u8313 
\f6 \uc0\u7580 \u7506 \u8319 \u7511 
\f3 . \'85one of the reasons for the victory of the States over the towns from the fifteenth century on is that the State alone has the faculty of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'approprier pleinement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the war machine \cf3 \strokec3 [appropriating to itself fully \'97 the \'b615 reflexive of taking-as-one's-own]\cf0 \strokec2 : by territorial recruitment of men, material investment, industrialization of war (it is in the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 manufactures d'armes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  more than in the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fabriques d'\'e9pingles
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [arms manufactories\'85 pin factories \'97 Adam Smith's pin factory: serial production and mechanical division born in the armory, not the pin-works \'97 political economy's founding example displaced]\cf0 \strokec2  that serial production and mechanical division appear). The commercial towns on the contrary need rapid wars, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 recourent \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  mercenaries \cf3 \strokec3 [have recourse to \'97 the legal recourse-idiom]\cf0 \strokec2 , and 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne peuvent qu'encaster
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the war machine \cf3 \strokec3 [can only encast \'97 the \'b62 coinage returned at the fn.'s point: the towns' constitutive limit stated in the emperor's verb]\cf0 \strokec2 .\
The problem of diffusion, of diffusionism, is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 mal pos\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [badly posed \'97 the problem-posing register (\'b612, probl\'e8me toujours pos\'e9): fault in the position, not the answer]\cf0 \strokec2  as long as one presupposes a center 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e0 partir duquel la diffusion se ferait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [from which the diffusion would make itself \'97 conditional + reflexive: the presupposed origin voiced hypothetically]\cf0 \strokec2 . There is diffusion only by 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 mise en communication
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [placing in communication \'97 the mise en X operative formula: communication as an act performed, not a state]\cf0 \strokec2  of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 potentiels
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of very different orders \cf3 \strokec3 [potentials \'97 the \'b616/\'b621 physics chain: diffusion as discharge between unequal potentials]\cf0 \strokec2 : all diffusion proceeds 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 au milieu, par le milieu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [in the middle, by the middle \'97 the milieu chain at full statement (\'b65, \'b620): the middle as both place and means]\cf0 \strokec2 , like everything that \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pousse
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb, of the rhizome type \cf3 \strokec3 [\'ab grows \'bb, pushes up \'97 pousser: the plant's push; the cross-plateau citation: grass, the Rhizome plateau's own figure, named in its home verb]\cf0 \strokec2 . An international ecumenical organization does not proceed from an imperial center that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'imposerait \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  an exterior milieu to homogenize it \cf3 \strokec3 [would impose itself on \'97 conditional + reflexive: the imperial reading refused in its own mood]\cf0 \strokec2 ; 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 elle ne se r\'e9duit pas davantage \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  relations between formations of the same order \cf3 \strokec3 [no more does it reduce itself to \'97 davantage (\'b614) + the reflexive r\'e9duire (\'b613)]\cf0 \strokec2 , for example between States (S.D.N., O.N.U.\'85). On the contrary, it constitutes an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 intermediate milieu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  between the different coexistent orders. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Aussi bien n'est-elle pas
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  exclusively economic or commercial, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 elle est aussi bien
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  religious, artistic, etc. \cf3 \strokec3 [just as well\'85 just as well \'97 the \'b619 equalizer doubled, with formal inversion: the registers leveled twice over]\cf0 \strokec2  It is in this sense that one will call international organization everything that has the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 aptitude de passer par
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  diverse social formations simultaneously \cf3 \strokec3 [aptitude to pass by way of \'97 the routing idiom as capacity: transit as the defining talent]\cf0 \strokec2 , States, towns, deserts, machines de guerre, primitive societies. The great historical commercial formations do not simply have city-poles, but primitive, imperial, nomad segments, by which they pass, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 quitte \'e0 ressortir sous une autre forme
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [at the cost of coming out again under another form \'97 quitte \'e0 (\'b620): the risk-idiom, transformation as the booked price of transit, not a chance outcome]\cf0 \strokec2 .\
