\'b2\'b2 Samir Amin analyzes this specificity of the \'ab peripheral formations \'bb of the Third World, and distinguishes two principal species of them, oriental and african, american: \'ab The Americas, Asia and the Arab Orient, black Africa were not transformed in the same manner, because they were not integrated at the same stage of capitalist development at the center and thus did not fill the same functions in this development \'bb (\ul \strokec2 Le d\'e9veloppement in\'e9gal\ulnone \strokec2 , pp. 257 ff.; and \ul \strokec2 L'accumulation \'e0 l'\'e9chelle mondiale\ulnone \strokec2 , \'c9d. Anthropos, pp. 373\'96376). 
