\f2 \cf2 des partenaires \'e9value d\'e8s le d\'e9but le volume ou la densit\'e9 du dernier mot qui lui donnerait l'avantage, et clorait la discussion, marquant la fin d'un exercice ou d'un cycle d'agencement, pour que tout puisse recommencer. Chacun calcule ses mots en fonction de l'\'e9valuation de ce dernier mot, et du temps vaguement convenu pour y atteindre. Et au-del\'e0 du dernier mot ( p\'e9nulti\'e8me) il y aurait d'autres mots encore, cette fois ultimes, qui feraient entrer dans un autre agencement, divorce par exemple, parce qu'on aurait d\'e9pass\'e9 la \'ab mesure \'bb . On en dira autant du dernier amour. Proust montrait comment un amour peut \'eatre orient\'e9 sur sa propre limite, sa propre marge : il r\'e9p\'e8te sa propre fin. Ensuite un nouvel amour, si bien que chaque amour est s\'e9riel, et qu'il y a aussi une s\'e9rie des amours. Mais, \'ab au-del\'e0 \'bb encore, il y a l'ultime, l\'e0 o\'f9 l'agencement change, l\'e0 o\'f9 l'agencement amoureux fait place \'e0 un agencement artistique - l'\'8cuvre \'e0 faire, le probl\'e8me de Proust . . . L'\'e9change est seulement une apparence : chaque partenaire ou chaque groupe appr\'e9cie la valeur du dernier objet r\'e9ceptible (objet-limite ), et l'\'e9quivalence apparente en d\'e9coule. L'\'e9galisation r\'e9sulte des deux s\'e9ries h\'e9t\'e9rog\'e8nes, l'\'e9change ou la communication r\'e9sulte des deux monologues (palabre) .
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 the last word that would give them the advantage and conclude the discussion, marking the end of an operation period or cycle of the assemblage, allowing it to start all over again. Both calculate their words in accordance with their evaluation of this last word, and the vaguely agreed time for it to come. And beyond the last (penultimate) word there lie still other words, this time final words that would cause them to enter another assemblage, di vorce, for example, because they would have overstepped "bounds." The same could be said for the last love. Proust has shown how a love can be oriented toward its own limit, its own margin: it repeats its own ending. A new love follows, so that each love is serial, so that there is a series of loves. But once again, "beyond" lies the ultimate, at the point where the assemblage changes, where the assemblage of love is superseded by an artistic assemblage-the Work to be written, which is the problem Proust tackles . . .
\f1 \

\f2 Exchange is only an appearance: each partner or group assesses the value of the last receivable object (limit-object), and the apparent equivalence derives from that. The equalization results from the two heterogeneous series, the exchange or communication results from two monologues (palabre).
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'85each of the partners evaluates 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e8s le d\'e9but
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [from the start \'97 the \'b613 formula (\'ab d\'e8s le d\'e9but \'bb), there scare-quoted for origins, here plain for the domestic scene]\cf0 \strokec2  the volume or the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 densit\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the last word \cf3 \strokec3 [density \'97 the physical measure (Rhizome \'b62b, teneur/density): words weighed as matter]\cf0 \strokec2  that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 lui donnerait l'avantage, et clorait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the discussion \cf3 \strokec3 [would give him the advantage, and would close \'97 clore: the formal closure-verb, sessions and debates; conditionals of the plan]\cf0 \strokec2 , marking the end of an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 exercice
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  or a cycle of agencement \cf3 \strokec3 [exercise \'97 the fiscal exercice again (\'b630): the quarrel keeps books too]\cf0 \strokec2 , 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pour que tout puisse recommencer
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [so that everything can recommence \'97 the recommencement law: the row's purpose is its own repetition]\cf0 \strokec2 . Each 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 calcule ses mots
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [calculates his words \'97 the compte chain: words counted out like coins against the last one]\cf0 \strokec2  
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en fonction de
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the evaluation of this last word, and of the time 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 vaguement convenu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  for reaching it \cf3 \strokec3 [vaguely agreed \'97 convenir: the pact-verb (\'b61, pacts and contracts): even the quarrel has its treaty-clock]\cf0 \strokec2 . And beyond the last word (penultimate) 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il y aurait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  still other words, this time ultimate, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 qui feraient entrer
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  into another agencement \cf3 \strokec3 [there would be\'85 which would make enter \'97 the conditional pair: the ultimate held in the mood of the not-yet]\cf0 \strokec2 , divorce for example, because 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 on aurait d\'e9pass\'e9 la \'ab mesure \'bb
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one would have exceeded the \'ab measure \'bb \'97 la mesure: the chain-word (\'b616 \'e0 mesure, \'b626 \'e0 la mesure de, \'b627 dans la mesure o\'f9) arriving scare-quoted: moderation, meter, and measurement in one, overstepped; the conjugal thread reaches its rupture]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 On en dira autant du dernier amour
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one will say as much of the last love \'97 the instruction-future of the dire-family (\'b63, \'b619 qui dira): the analysis extended by decree]\cf0 \strokec2 . Proust 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 montrait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  how a love can be oriented on its own limit, its own margin: it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 r\'e9p\'e8te sa propre fin
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [repeats its own end \'97 the limit-law in the imperfect of Proust's demonstration]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ensuite un nouvel amour
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [then a new love \'97 the verbless fragment: succession stated without a verb, love following like an entry in a list]\cf0 \strokec2 , so that each love is serial, and there is also a series of loves. But, \'ab beyond \'bb again, there is the ultimate, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l\'e0 o\'f9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the agencement changes, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l\'e0 o\'f9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the amorous agencement 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fait place \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  an artistic agencement \cf3 \strokec3 [there where\'85 there where\'85 makes place for \'97 the doubled l\'e0 o\'f9; faire place (\'b65): the yielding-of-place idiom: love steps aside for the work]\cf0 \strokec2  \'97 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'\'8cuvre \'e0 faire
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , the problem of Proust\'85 \cf3 \strokec3 [the Work to-be-made \'97 faire: making, not only writing; \'e0 faire: the yet-to-do, the Work as standing task]\cf0 \strokec2  Exchange is only an appearance: each partner or each group 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 appr\'e9cie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the value of the last receivable object (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 objet-limite
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ) \cf3 \strokec3 [appraises \'97 the assessor's verb: valuation as official act]\cf0 \strokec2 , and the apparent equivalence 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en d\'e9coule
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [flows from it \'97 d\'e9couler: the couler chain (\'b67): equivalence as runoff, not foundation]\cf0 \strokec2 . Equalization results from the two heterogeneous series, exchange or communication results from the two monologues (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 palabre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ) \cf3 \strokec3 [palaver \'97 palabre: the drawn-out parley, interminable negotiation-talk: exchange as two speeches passing]\cf0 \strokec2 .\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

