\f2 \cf2 \'b633 fr.546 umn.439
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 Il n'y a ni valeur d'\'e9change ni valeur d'usage, mais \'e9valuation du dernier de chaque c\'f4t\'e9 (calcul de risque aff\'e9rent \'e0 un franchissement de la limite), une \'e9valuation-anticipation qui rend compte du caract\'e8re rituel autant qu'utilitaire, du caract\'e8re s\'e9riel autant qu'\'e9changiste. L'\'e9valuation de la limite pour chacun des groupes est pr\'e9sente d\'e8s le d\'e9but, et commande d\'e9j\'e0 le premier \'ab \'e9change \'bb entre les deux. Certes, il y a bien un t\'e2tonnement, l'\'e9valuation n'est pas s\'e9parable d'un t\'e2tonnement collectif. Mais celui-ci ne porte pas du tout sur la quantit\'e9 de travail social, il porte sur l'id\'e9e du dernier d'un c\'f4t\'e9 comme de l'autre, et se fait \'e0 vitesse variable, mais toujours plus rapide que le temps n\'e9cessaire pour arriver effectivement au dernier objet ou m\'eame pour passer d'une op\'e9ration \'e0 une autre 24. C'est en ce sens que l'\'e9valuation est essentiellement anticipante, d\'e9j\'e0 pr\'e9sente dans les premiers 24. Sur l'importance d'une th\'e9orie de l'\'e9valuation et du t\'e2tonnement dans le marginalisme, cf. l'expos\'e9 critique de Fradin, Les fondements logiques de la th\'e9orie n\'e9oclassique de l'\'e9change, Maspero. Pour les marxistes, il y a bien aussi une \'e9valuation t\'e2tonnante, mais qui ne peut porter que sur la quantit\'e9 de trvail socialement n\'e9cessaire ; Engels en parle, pr\'e9cis\'e9ment \'e0 propos des soci\'e9t\'e9s pr\'e9capitalistes. Il invoque \'ab un proc\'e8s d'approximation en zigzag, de nombreux t\'e2tonnements dans le noir \'bb, qui se r\'e8glent plus ou moins sur \'ab la n\'e9cessit\'e9 pour chacun de rentrer finalement dans ses frais \'bb (on se demandera si ce dernier membre de phrase ne reconstitue pas une sorte de crit\'e8re marginaliste). Cf. Engels, pr\'e9face au Capital, livre III, Ed. Sociales, pp. 32-34. termes de la s\'e9rie.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 There is neither exchange value nor use value but rather an evaluation of the last by both parties (a calculation of the risk involved in crossing the limit), an anticipation-evaluation that takes into account the ritual character as well as the utilitarian, the serial character as well as the exchangist. The evaluation of the limit is there from the start in both groups, and already governs the first "exchange" between them. Of course there is groping in the dark; the evaluation is inseparable from a collective feeling out. But it does not bear on the quantity of social labor but on the idea of the last on both sides; the speed with which it is accomplished varies, but it is always done faster than the time necessary effectively to arrive at the last object, or even to pass from one operation to another.25 This is the sense in which the evaluation is essentially anticipatory, that it is already present in the first terms of the series.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 There is neither exchange value nor 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 valeur d'usage
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [use value \'97 the Marxian pair dismissed together; usage: the \'b69 register (pr\'eat d'usage), use as legal enjoyment]\cf0 \strokec2 , but evaluation of the last on each side (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 calcul de risque aff\'e9rent \'e0 un franchissement de la limite
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [calculation of risk afferent to a crossing of the limit \'97 aff\'e9rent: the administrative "pertaining to," the file's own adjective; franchissement: from franchir, to cross freely \'97 the affranchi root (\'b622): crossing and enfranchisement one family]\cf0 \strokec2 ), an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9valuation-anticipation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [evaluation-anticipation \'97 the compound family (\'b624 conjuration-anticipation, \'b628 anticipation-conjuration): anticipation now paired with its economic face]\cf0 \strokec2  that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rend compte du
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  ritual character as much as the utilitarian \cf3 \strokec3 [renders account of \'97 rendre compte: the bookkeeping idiom for explanation itself: the theory too must balance its books]\cf0 \strokec2 , the serial character as much as the exchangist. The evaluation of the limit is present 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e8s le d\'e9but
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  for each of the two groups, and 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 commande d\'e9j\'e0 le premier \'ab \'e9change \'bb
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [already commands the first \'ab exchange \'bb \'97 d\'e9j\'e0 + premier: the \'b68 question (what is first?) answered \'97 the last comes first; commander: the \'b611 register, value commanded]\cf0 \strokec2  between the two. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Certes, il y a bien un t\'e2tonnement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [certainly, there is indeed a groping \'97 t\'e2tonnement: feeling one's way in the dark, trial by touch: the concessive grant (\'b63, il est bien vrai)]\cf0 \strokec2 , the evaluation is not separable from a collective t\'e2tonnement. But this one 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne porte pas du tout sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the quantity of social labor, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il porte sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the idea of the last on one side as on the other \cf3 \strokec3 [does not bear at all on\'85 it bears on \'97 the porter sur pair again (\'b630): the weight relocated]\cf0 \strokec2 , and 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se fait \'e0 vitesse variable
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [makes itself at variable speed \'97 the reflexive + vitesse: evaluation as self-executing process with a speed, the book's opening obsession (Rhizome \'b62a, dates and speeds)]\cf0 \strokec2 , but always more rapid than the time necessary to 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 arriver effectivement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  at the last object \cf3 \strokec3 [effectively arrive \'97 arriver (\'b617): the evaluation outrunning the arrival it evaluates \'97 anticipation as head start]\cf0 \strokec2  or even to pass from one operation to another\'b2
\f5 \uc0\u8308 
\f3 . It is in this sense that the evaluation is essentially 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 anticipante, d\'e9j\'e0 pr\'e9sente dans les premiers termes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the series \cf3 \strokec3 [anticipating, already present in the first terms \'97 the plateau's three chains (anticipation, d\'e9j\'e0, premier) closed in one clause]\cf0 \strokec2 .\
\'b2
\f5 \uc0\u8308 
\f3  On the importance of a theory of evaluation and t\'e2tonnement in marginalism, cf. the critical exposition of Fradin, \ul \strokec2 Les fondements logiques de la th\'e9orie n\'e9oclassique de l'\'e9change\ulnone \strokec2 , Maspero. For the Marxists, there is indeed also a groping evaluation, but which can bear only on the quantity of socially necessary labor; Engels speaks of it, precisely in connection with precapitalist societies. He 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 invoque
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [invokes \'97 the summons-verb (\'b66\'967): Engels called as witness]\cf0 \strokec2  \'ab a process of approximation 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en zigzag
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , numerous 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 t\'e2tonnements
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  in the dark \'bb \cf3 \strokec3 [in zigzag \'97 Engels's own word: the \'b611/\'b615 zigzag vocabulary revealed at its source]\cf0 \strokec2 , which regulate themselves more or less on \'ab the necessity for each 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 de rentrer finalement dans ses frais
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb \cf3 \strokec3 [to recover his costs in the end \'97 rentrer dans ses frais: the accounting idiom, to break even: the compte chain in Engels's mouth]\cf0 \strokec2  (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 on se demandera si ce dernier membre de phrase
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  does not reconstitute a sort of marginalist criterion) \cf3 \strokec3 [one will ask oneself whether this last limb-of-sentence \'97 membre de phrase: the sentence's own anatomy; and dernier: D&G applying the plateau's concept to Engels's syntax \'97 the last clause as the marginal clause, evaluated last, commanding the whole]\cf0 \strokec2 . Cf. Engels, preface to \ul \strokec2 Capital\ulnone \strokec2 , book III, \'c9d. Sociales, pp. 32\'9634. 
