\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , its desirability, on both sides. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Encore faut-il
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  a condition \cf3 \strokec3 [still must there be \'97 the inversion-idiom of the additional requirement: the argument demanding one more premise]\cf0 \strokec2  that gives a proper interest to the stock, a proper desirability (otherwise, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 on d\'e9truirait, on consumerait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the objects rather than stock them: 
