\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one would destroy, one would consume-by-fire\'85 consumation \'97 consumer, not consommer: burning up, wasting in flame; the word is Bataille's \'97 consumation as glorious expenditure, d\'e9pense: destruction as the primitive answer to the stock]\cf0 \strokec2  is in effect the means for the primitive groups of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 conjurer
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the stock, and of maintaining their agencement). The stock depends itself on a new type of agencement. And doubtless there is much ambiguity in these expressions \'ab apr\'e8s \'bb, \'ab nouveau \'bb, \'ab 
