\f6 \cf2 ) Bernard Schmitt a propos\'e9 u n mod\'e8le d'appareil d e capture qui rend compte des op\'e9rations de comparaison et d'appropriation. Sans doute ce mod\'e8le est-il construit en fonction de la monnaie, en \'e9conomie capitaliste. Mais il semble reposer sur des principes abstraits qui d\'e9bordent ces limites 33 . - A. On part d'un flux indivis, qui n'est encore ni appropri\'e9 ni compar\'e9, \'ab dispo33. Bernard Schmitt, Monnaie, salaires et profits. nibilit\'e9 pure \'bb, \'ab non-possession et non-richesse \'bb : c'est pr\'e9cis\'e9ment ce qui arrive dans une cr\'e9ation de monnaie par les banques, mais c'est plus g\'e9n\'e9ralement la d\'e9termination du stock, cr\'e9ation d'un flux indivis. - B . Le flux indivis se divise pour autant qu'il est distribu\'e9 aux \'ab facteurs \'bb, r\'e9parti entre les \'ab facteurs \'bb . Il n'y a qu'une seule sorte de facteurs, les producteurs imm\'e9diats. On peut les appeler les \'ab pauvres \'bb, et dire que le flux est r\'e9parti entre les pauvres. Mais ce ne serait pas exact, puisqu'il n'y a pas de \'ab riches \'bb pr\'e9alables. Ce qui compte, ce qui est important, c'est que les producteurs n'acqui\'e8rent pas encore la possession de ce qui leur est distribu\'e9, et que ce qui leur est distribu\'e9 n'est pas encore une richesse : la r\'e9mun\'e9ration ne suppose ni comparaison ni appropriation, ni vente-achat, c'est beaucoup plus une op\'e9ration du type nexum. Il y a seulement \'e9galit\'e9 de l'ensemble B et de l'ensemble A, de l'ensemble r\'e9parti et de l'ensemble indivis. On peut appeler salaire nominal l 'ensemble r\'e9parti, si bien que les salaires nominaux sont la forme d'expression de tout l'ensemble indivis (<< l'enti\'e8re expression nominale \'bb, ou, comme on dit souvent, \'ab l'expression de tout le revenu national \'bb) : l'appareil de capture appara\'eet ici comme s\'e9miologique. - C.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Bernard Schmitt has proposed a model of the apparatus of capture that takes into account the operations of comparison and appropriation. This model admittedly revolves around money as a capitalist economics. But it seems to be based on abstract principles that transcend these limits.38<br>A. The point of departure is an undivided flow that has yet to be appropriated or compared, a "pure availability," "non possession and nonwealth": this is precisely what occurs when banks create money, but taken more generally it is the establishment of the stock, which is the creation of an undivided flow.<br>B. The undivided flow becomes divided to the extent it is allocated to the "factors," distributed to the "factors." There is only one kind of factor, the immediate producers. We could call them the "poor" and say that the flow is distributed among the poor. But this would be inaccurate because there are no preexistent "rich." What counts, the important thing, is that the producers do not yet acquire possession of what is distributed to them, and that what is distributed to them is not yet wealth: remuneration assumes neither comparison and appropriation, nor buying-selling; it is much more an operation of the nexum type. There is only equality between set B and set A, between the distributed set and the undivided set. The distributed set could be called nominal wage; nominal wages are the form of expression of the entire undivided set ("the entire nominal expression," or as it is often put, "the expression of total national income"). This is the point at which the apparatus of capture becomes semiological.<br>38. Bernard Schmitt, Monnaie, salaires et profits.
\f1 \cell 
