\f6 \cf2 \'b655 fr.559 umn.448
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Il ne cr\'e9e pas la forme mon\'e9taire de l'imp\'f4t sans que des flux de monnaie ne fuient, et n'alimentent ou ne fassent na\'eetre d'autres puissances (notamment dans le commerce et la banque) . Et, surtout, il ne cr\'e9e pas le syst\'e8me de sa propri\'e9t\'e9 publique sans qu'un flux d'appropriation priv\'e9e n'en sorte \'e0 c\'f4t\'e9, et ne se mette \'e0 couler hors de sa prise : cette propri\'e9t\'e9 priv\'e9e ne d\'e9coule pas elle-m\'eame du syst\'e8me archa\'efque, mais se constitue marginalement, d'une mani\'e8re d'autant plus n\'e9cessaire, in\'e9vitable, \'e0 travers les mailles du surcodage. T\'fckei est sans doute celui qui a pos\'e9 le plus s\'e9rieusement le probl\'e8me d'une origine de la propri\'e9t\'e9 priv\'e9e, en fonction d'un syst\'e8me qui semble l'exclure de toutes parts . Car celle-ci ne peut na\'eetre ni du c\'f4t\'e9 de l'empereur-despote, ni du c\'f4t\'e9 des paysans, dont la part d'autonomie est li\'e9e \'e0 la possession communale, ni du c\'f4t\'e9 des fonctionnaires qui trouvent la base de leur existence et de leur revenu dans cette forme communale publique (<< les aristocrates peuvent dans ces conditions devenir de petits despotes, mais non pas des propri\'e9taires priv\'e9s \'bb ). M\'eame les esclaves appartiennent \'e0 la commune ou \'e0 la fonction publique. La question devient donc : y a-t-il des gens qui sont constitu\'e9s dans l'empire surcodant, mais constitu\'e9s comme exclus et d\'e9cod\'e9s, n\'e9cessairement ? La r\'e9ponse de Tokei, c'est l'esclave affranchi. C'est lui qui n'a plus de place. C'est lui qui lance ses lamentations dans tout l'empire chinois : la plainte ( \'e9l\'e9gie) a toujours \'e9t\'e9 facteur politique. Mais c'est lui aussi qui forme les premiers germes de propri\'e9t\'e9 priv\'e9e, d\'e9veloppe le commerce, et invente dans la m\'e9tallurgie un esclavage priv\'e9 dont il sera le nouveau ma\'eetre 36.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 It does not create the monetary form of the tax without flows of money escaping, and nourishing or bringing into being other powers (notably in commerce and banking). And above all, it does not created a system of public property without a flow of private appropriation growing up beside it, then beginning to pass beyond its grasp; this private property does not itself issue from the archaic system but is constituted on the margins, all the more necessarily and inevitably, slipping through the net of overcoding. It is undoubtedly Tokei who has formulated the problem of an origin of private property in the most serious way, in the context of a system that seems to exclude it from every angle. For private property can arise neither on the side of the emperor-despot not on the side of the peasants, whose autonomy is tied to communal possession, nor on the side of the functionaries whose existence and income are based on that public communal form ("the aristocrats can under these conditions become petty despots but not private landowners"). Even the slaves belong to the community or the public function. The question then becomes, Are there people who are constituted in the overcoding empire, but constituted as necessarily excluded and decoded? Tokei's answer is the freed slaves. It is they who have no place. It is their lamentations that are heard the length and breadth of the Chinese Empire: the plaint (elegy) has always been a political factor. But it is also they who form the first seeds of private property, who develop trade, and with metallurgy invent a kind of private slavery in which they will be the new master.41
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 t does not create the monetary form of the tax 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 sans que des flux de monnaie ne fuient, et n'alimentent ou ne fassent na\'eetre d'autres puissances
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [without flows of money fleeing, and feeding or making be born other powers \'97 fuir again + alimenter, the nourishment register + faire na\'eetre: money escaping to feed rival births]\cf0 \strokec2  (notably in commerce and banking). And, above all, it does not create the system of its public property without a flow of private appropriation 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 sortant \'e0 c\'f4t\'e9, et ne se mette \'e0 couler hors de sa prise
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [coming out beside it, and setting about flowing outside its grasp \'97 \'e0 c\'f4t\'e9 (\'b615): the lateral position again; se mettre \'e0 (\'b614): the onset idiom; couler: the hydraulic chain at its most literal \'97 private property as leak; prise: the capture-noun (\'b618 fn., \'b620, \'b626) \'97 out of the hold, escaping the very grip the plateau is named for]\cf0 \strokec2 : this private property does not itself 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e9coule
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  from the archaic system, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se constitue marginalement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [constitutes itself marginally \'97 the marginalism chain (\'b630\'9631): property born at the margin, the economic concept become topology]\cf0 \strokec2 , in a manner 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d'autant plus
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  necessary, inevitable, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e0 travers les mailles du surcodage
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [all the more \'97 the proportional chain; through the meshes of the overcoding \'97 mailles: the \'b67 sentence reprised almost verbatim (property flows through the State's meshes): the plateau quoting itself across forty-eight paragraphs]\cf0 \strokec2 . T\'f6kei is doubtless the one who has 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pos\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  most seriously the problem of an origin of private property, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en fonction d'un
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  system that seems to exclude it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 de toutes parts
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . For it can 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 na\'eetre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  neither on the side of the emperor-despot, nor on the side of the peasants, whose part of autonomy is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 li\'e9e
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  to communal possession \cf3 \strokec3 [tied \'97 the lier chain, in property form]\cf0 \strokec2 , nor on the side of the functionaries who find the base of their existence and their 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 revenu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  in this communal public form (\'ab the aristocrats can in these conditions become petty despots, but not private proprietors \'bb). Even the slaves belong to the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 commune
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  or to the public 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fonction
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . The question therefore becomes: are there people who are constituted in the overcoding empire, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 constitu\'e9s comme exclus et d\'e9cod\'e9s, n\'e9cessairement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  ? \cf3 \strokec3 [constituted as excluded and decoded, necessarily \'97 the participle doing the work: exclusion as a mode of constitution, made not found]\cf0 \strokec2  T\'f6kei's answer is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'esclave affranchi
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the freed slave \'97 affranchi: the manumission chain's literal referent at last (\'b622 towns affranchies, \'b633 franchissement): after freed cities and crossed limits, the freedman himself; collective singular, a personage]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is he who no longer has a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 place
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [place \'97 the faire place chain inverted: the one for whom no place was made]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is he who 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 lance ses lamentations
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  across the whole Chinese empire: 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 la plainte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  (\'e9l\'e9gie) has always been a political factor \cf3 \strokec3 [the plaint \'97 plainte: the lament and the legal complaint (porter plainte, to file suit): elegy as litigation, grief with standing]\cf0 \strokec2 . But it is he also who forms the first 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 germes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of private property \cf3 \strokec3 [germs, seeds \'97 the \'b64 J\'fcnger germes: the world's mutilated seed-stock, now sprouting property]\cf0 \strokec2 , develops commerce, and invents in metallurgy a private slavery of which he will be the new 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ma\'eetre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 \'b3
\f5 \uc0\u8310 
\f3 .\
\'b3
