\f6 \cf2 \'b656 fr.560 umn.449
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Nous avons vu pr\'e9c\'e9demment le r\'f4le de l'esclave affranchi dans la machine de guerre, pour la formation du corps sp\'e9cial. C'est sous une autre forme, et avec de tout autres raisons, qu'il a tant d'importance dans l'appareil d'Etat, et dans l'\'e9volution de cet appareil, pour la formation d'un corps priv\'e9. Les deux aspects peuvent se r\'e9unir, mais renvoient \'e0 deux lign\'e9es diff\'e9ren tes . Ce qui compte, ce n'est donc pas le cas particulier de l'esclave affranchi . Ce qui compte, c'est le personnage collectif de l'Exclu. Ce qui compte, c'est que, d'une mani\'e8re ou d'une autre, l'appareil de surcodage suscite des flux eux-m\'eames d\'e9cod\'e9s - de monnaie, de travail, de propri\'e9t\'e9 . . . Ceux-ci sont le corr\'e9lat de celui-l\'e0. Et la corr\'e9lation n'est pas seulement sociale, \'e0 l'int\'e9rieur de l'empire archa\'efque, elle est aussi g\'e9ographique. Ce serait le moment de reprendre la confrontation de l'Orient et de l'Occident. Suivant la grande th\'e8se arch\'e9ologique de Gordon Childe, l'Etat imp\'e9rial archa\'efque implique un surplus agricole stock\'e9, qui va rendre possible l'entretien d'un corps sp\'e9cialis\'e9 d'artisans rn\'e9tallurgistes et commer\'e7ants. En effet, le surplus comme contenu propre du surcodage ne doit pas seulement \'eatre stock\'e9, mais absorb\'e9, consomm\'e9, r\'e9alis\'e9. Sans doute cette exigence \'e9conomique d'une absorption du surplus est un des principaux aspects de l'appropriation de la machine de guerre par l'Etat imp\'e9rial : d\'e8s le d\'e9but, l'institution militaire est un des plus forts moyens 36. Tokei, \'ab Les conditions de la propri\'e9t\'e9 fonci\'e8re dans la Chine de l'\'e9poque Tcheou \'bb, Acta antiqua 1958. Marx et Engels rappelaient d\'e9j\'e0 que la pl\'e8be romaine (partiellement constitu\'e9e d'affranchis publics) avait seule \'ab le droit d'assigner la propri\'e9t\'e9 de l'ager publicus \'bb : les pl\'e9b\'e9iens devenaient propri\'e9taires priv\'e9s de biens fonciers, comme de richesses marchandes et artisanales, pr\'e9cis\'e9ment en tant qu'ils \'e9taient \'ab exclus de tous les droits publics \'bb (cf. Marx, Grundrisse, Pl\'e9iade II, p. 319, Engels, Origine de la famille, Ed. Sociales, p. 1 19). d'absorber le surplus.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 We saw previously the role played by freed slaves in the war machine, in the formation of the special body. It is in a different form, and following entirely different principles, that they play an important role in the State apparatus and in the evolution of that apparatus, this time in the formation of a private body. The two aspects can combine, but they belong to two different lines.<br>What counts is not the particular case of the freed slave.What counts is the collective figure of the Outsider. What counts is that in one way or another the apparatus of overcoding gives rise to flows that are themselves decoded-flows of money, labor, property . . . These flows are the correlate of the apparatus. And the correlation is not only social, internal to the archaic empire, it is also geographical. This would be the place to bring up 450 D 7000 B.c.: APPARATUS OF CAPTURE the confrontation between the East and the West. According to V. Gordon Childe's great archaeological thesis, the archaic imperial State implies a stockpiled agricultural surplus, which makes possible the maintenance of a specialized body of mercantile and metallurgical artisans. Indeed, the surplus as the content proper to overcoding must be not only stockpiled but absorbed, consumed, realized. Doubtless, this economic requirement that the surplus be absorbed is one of the principal aspects of the appropriation of the war machine by the imperial State: The military institution is from the start one of the most effective means of absorbing surplus.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 We have seen previously the role of the esclave affranchi in the machine de guerre, for the formation of the special 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 corps
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . It is under another form, and with entirely other 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 raisons
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , that he has such importance in the State apparatus, and in the evolution of that apparatus, for the formation of a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 corps priv\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [private body \'97 corps: the body doubled: special body (war machine) / private body (State) \'97 the freedman as former of bodies]\cf0 \strokec2 . The two aspects can reunite, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 renvoient \'e0 deux lign\'e9es diff\'e9rentes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [refer back to two different lineages \'97 renvoyer + lign\'e9es: the \'b68 lineage-codes word: the freedman with two genealogies, not two lines]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce qui compte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , is thus not the particular case of the freed slave. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce qui compte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , is the collective 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 personnage
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'Exclu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [what counts \'97 the compter anaphora, tripled: the counting-verb marshaling the argument; the collective personage of the Excluded One \'97 capital E: a conceptual persona, one who is constituted-as-excluded (\'b655's participle), the empire's own product \'97 not an outsider who was never in]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce qui compte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , is that, in one manner or another, the apparatus of surcodage 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 suscite
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  flows themselves decoded \'97 of money, of labor, of property\'85 \cf3 \strokec3 [calls forth \'97 susciter: the raising-up verb at its thesis-station; the triad again: the trinity formula's three columns, now as escapees]\cf0 \strokec2  These are the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 corr\'e9lat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of that. And the correlation is not only social, interior to the archaic empire, it is also geographical. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce serait le moment de reprendre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the confrontation of the Orient and the Occident \cf3 \strokec3 [this would be the moment to take up again \'97 conditional of the program, held]\cf0 \strokec2 . Following the great archaeological thesis of Gordon Childe, the archaic imperial State implies a stocked agricultural surplus, which will render possible 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'entretien
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of a specialized corps \cf3 \strokec3 [the maintenance \'97 entretenir (\'b610, \'b613): the State as provisioner again]\cf0 \strokec2  of metallurgist and merchant artisans. In effect, the surplus as 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 contenu propre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the surcodage \cf3 \strokec3 [proper content \'97 the \'b646 content/expression pair: surplus as what overcoding expresses]\cf0 \strokec2  must not only be stocked, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 absorb\'e9, consomm\'e9, r\'e9alis\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [absorbed, consumed, realized \'97 consomm\'e9, the ordinary consumption-verb: note against \'b635, where D&G wrote consumer/consumation \'97 the two verbs coexist in the plateau, confirming the \'b635 choice as marked, Bataillean, deliberate]\cf0 \strokec2 . Doubtless this economic exigency of an absorption of the surplus is one of the principal aspects of the appropriation of the machine de guerre by the imperial State: 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e8s le d\'e9but
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , the military institution is one of the strongest 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 moyens
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of absorbing the surplus.\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

