\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  raw materials \cf3 \strokec3 [against \'97 the barter contre: exchange as counter-position]\cf0 \strokec2 , even come from central and western Europe (notably wood and metals). Certainly, the Orient must ceaselessly reproduce its stocks; but, formally, 
