\f6 \cf2 ( :' l' s l comme si le m\'eame probl\'e8me avait re\'e7u deux solutions, Lt sol l l t ion d'Orient, puis celle d'Occident qui se greffe sur la J ll'l' I l l it:re et la sort de l'impasse, tout en la supposant . Le m\'e9tall mg i s t c c t le commer\'e7ant europ\'e9ens ou europ\'e9anis\'e9s vont se trouVLT devant un march\'e9 international beaucoup moins cod\'e9, qui li l' sc l i mite pas \'e0 une maison ou classe imp\'e9riales. Et, comme dit C1 l i l dc , les Etats \'e9g\'e9ens et occidentaux seront pris d\'e8s le d\'e9but d a n s un syst\'e8me \'e9conomique supra-national : ils baignent dedans, <I l l 1 i cu de le main tenir dans les limites de leurs propres mailles 37 . C 'est bien un autre p\'f4le d'Etat qui surgit, et qu'on peut d\'e9fin i r sommairement. La sph\'e8re publique ne caract\'e9rise plus la nature objective de la propri\'e9t\'e9, mais est plut\'f4t le moyen commlln d'une appropriation devenue priv\'e9e ; on entre ainsi dans les mi xtes public-priv\'e9 qui constituent le monde moderne. Le lien devient personnel ; des rapports personnels de d\'e9pendance, \'e0 la fois entre propri\'e9taires (contrats ), et entre propri\'e9t\'e9s et propri\'e9taires (conventions ), doublent ou remplacent les relations communautaires et de fonction ; m\'eame l'esclavage ne d\'e9flnit plus la disposition publique du travailleur communal, mais la propri\'e9t\'e9 priv\'e9e qui s'exerce sur des travailleurs individuels 38 . Le droit tout entier subit une mutation, et devient droit subjectif, conjonctif, \'ab topique \'bb : c'est que l'appareil d'Etat se trouve devant une nouvelle t\'e2che, qui consiste moins \'e0 surcoder des flux d\'e9j\'e0 cod\'e9s qu '\'e0 organiser des conjonctions de flux d\'e9cod\'e9s comme tels. Le r\'e9gime des signes a donc chang\'e9 : \'e0 tous ces \'e9gards, l'op\'e9ration du \'ab signifiant \'bb
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 It is as if two solutions were found for the same problem, the Oriental solution and then the Western one, which grafts itself upon the first and brings it out of the impasse while continuing to presuppose it. The European metallurgist and merchant faced a much less thoroughly coded international market, one not limited to an imperial house or class. And as Childe said, the Western and Aegean States were immersed in a supranational economic system from the start; they bathed in it, instead of containing it within the limits of their own net.42<br>It is indeed another pole of the State that arises, one that could be defined in summary fashion as follows. The public sphere no longer characterizes the objective nature of property but is instead the shared means for a now private appropriation; this yields the public-private mixes constitutive of the modern world. The bond becomes personal; personal relations of dependence, both between owners (contracts) and between owned and owners (conventions), parallel or replace community relations or relations based on one's public function. Even slavery changes; it no longer defines the public availability of the communal worker but rather private property as applied to individual workers.43 The law in its entirety undergoes a mutation, becoming subjective, conjunctive, "topical" law: this is because the State apparatus is faced with a new task, which consists less in overcoding already coded flows than in organizing con junctions of decoded flows as such. Thus the regime of signs has changed: in all of these respects, the operation of the imperial "signifier" has been superseded by processes ofsub jectification; machinic enslavement tends to be replaced by a regime of social sub jection.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It is as if the same problem had received two 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 solutions
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , the solution of the Orient, then that of the Occident which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se greffe sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the first \cf3 \strokec3 [grafts itself onto \'97 greffer: the horticultural graft, the West as scion on the oriental stock; also la greffe, the court clerk's office \'97 the graft filed]\cf0 \strokec2  and brings it out of the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 impasse
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 tout en la supposant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . The European or Europeanized metallurgist and merchant will find themselves before an international market much less coded, which does not limit itself to an imperial house or class. And, as Childe says, the Aegean and Western States 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 seront pris d\'e8s le d\'e9but
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  in a supra-national economic system \cf3 \strokec3 [will be taken, caught from the start \'97 pris: the capture-verb turned around: the capturing States themselves captured in a system they cannot hold]\cf0 \strokec2 : 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ils baignent dedans, au lieu de le maintenir dans les limites de leurs propres mailles
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 \'b3
\f5 \uc0\u8311 
\f3  \cf3 \strokec3 [they bathe in it, instead of maintaining it within the limits of their own meshes \'97 baigner: full immersion; mailles: the \'b67/\'b655 mesh-chain inverted \'97 the State's net too small for the sea it swims in]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is indeed 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 un autre p\'f4le d'\'c9tat qui surgit
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [another pole of State that looms up \'97 Proposition X's two poles returning as the argument's frame, with the surgir apparition-verb]\cf0 \strokec2 , and which one can define summarily. The public sphere no longer characterizes the objective nature of property, but is rather 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 le moyen commun
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of an appropriation 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 devenue priv\'e9e
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the common means of an appropriation become private \'97 devenu: the becoming in the past participle]\cf0 \strokec2 ; one thus enters the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 mixtes public-priv\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  that constitute the modern world. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Le lien devient personnel
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the bond becomes personal \'97 the \'b61 lien: the emperor's magic bond mutating into personal dependence, the binding-chain's modern station (terminus at \'b663)]\cf0 \strokec2 ; personal 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rapports de d\'e9pendance
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , at once between proprietors (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 contrats
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ), and between properties and proprietors (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 conventions
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ) \cf3 \strokec3 [contracts\'85 conventions \'97 the \'b61 jurist's instruments (treaties, pacts, contracts) redistributed; between properties and proprietors: the French pairs things and persons, not two classes of person]\cf0 \strokec2 , 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 doublent ou remplacent
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the communitarian and function relations \cf3 \strokec3 [double or replace \'97 doubler: the understudy register: the new relations standing in before supplanting]\cf0 \strokec2 ; even slavery no longer defines the public 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 disposition
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the communal worker \cf3 \strokec3 [disposition \'97 disposer (\'b65): the having-at-disposal: the worker as what the commune disposed of]\cf0 \strokec2 , but the private property that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'exerce sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  individual workers\'b3
\f5 \uc0\u8312 
\f3  \cf3 \strokec3 [exercises itself upon \'97 the \'b652\'9653 formula: property working its object]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Le droit tout entier subit une mutation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , and becomes subjective, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 conjonctif
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 topique
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb law \cf3 \strokec3 [conjunctive, \'ab topical \'bb \'97 topique: the rhetorician's topos and the physician's topical, local application: law by sites]\cf0 \strokec2 : it is that the State apparatus finds itself before a new task, which consists less in overcoding flows already coded than in 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 organiser des conjonctions de flux d\'e9cod\'e9s comme tels
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [organizing conjunctions of decoded flows as such \'97 conjonction: the marked term, topical knotting \'97 held apart from the conjugaison to come (\'b662): the distinction \'b623 flagged, about to be deployed by the text itself]\cf0 \strokec2 . The regime of signs has therefore changed: in all these regards, the operation of the imperial \'ab signifier \'bb 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fait place \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  processes of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 subjectivation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 ; 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'asservissement machinique
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  tends to be replaced by a regime of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 assujettissement social
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [machinic enslavement\'85 social subjection \'97 the pair: asservir (the servomechanism, \'b68) vs. assujettir (the making-subject, \'b623 r\'e9assujetti): two bondages, machine-part and subject]\cf0 \strokec2 .\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

