\f6 \cf2 \'b661 fr.563 umn.451
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Et la question de savoir si ces derni\'e8res formations r\'e9pondent encore au concept d'Etat ne peut \'eatre pos\'e9e que compte tenu de certaines corr\'e9lations : tout autant que les empires \'e9volu\'e9s, les cit\'e9s et les f\'e9odalit\'e9s supposent un empire archa\'efque qui leur sert de fond ; elles sont elles-m\'eames en contact avec des empires \'e9volu\'e9s qui r\'e9agissent sur elles ; elles pr\'e9parent activement des formes nouvelles d'Etat ( par exemple, la monarchie absolue comme aboutissement d 'un droit subjectif et d'un processus f\'e9odal 40). En effet, dans le riche domaine des rapports personnels, ce qui compte, ce n'est pas le caprice ou la variabilit\'e9 des personnes , mais la consistance des rapports, et l'ad\'e9quation d'une subjectivit\'e9 qui peut aller jusqu'au d\'e9lire, avec des actes qualifi\'e9s qui sont sources de droits et d'obligations . Dans une belle page, Edgar Quinet soulignait cette cO\'efncidence entre \'ab le d\'e9lire des douze Cesars et l '\'e2ge d'or du droit romain 41 \'bb . O r les subjectivations, les conjonctions, les appropriations n 'emp\'eachent pas les flux d\'e9cod\'e9s de continuer \'e0 couler, et d'engendrer sans cesse de nouveaux flux qui s'\'e9chappent ( nous l 'avons vu par exemple, au niveau d'une micropolitique au Moyen Age). C'est m\'eame l'\'e9quivoque de ces appareils : \'e0 la fois ils ne fonctionnent qu'avec des flux d\'e9cod\'e9s, et pourtant ne les laissent pas concourir ensemble, op\'e8re les conjonctions topiques qui valent pour autant de n\'9cuds ou recodages. D 'o\'f9 l'impression des historiens quand ils disent que le capitalisme \'ab aurait pu \'bb se produire d\'e8s ce moment-l\'e0 - en Chine, \'e0 Rome, \'e0 Byzance, au Moyen Age - que les conditions en \'e9taient donn\'e9es, mais qu'elles n '\'e9taient pas effectu\'e9es ni m\'eame effectuables .
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 The question as to whether these last-mentioned formations still answer to the concept of the State can be formulated only after certain correlations have been taken into account. Every bit as much as the evolved 452 0 7000 B.C.: APPARA TUS OF CAPTURE empires, the autonomous cities, and feudal systems presuppose an archaic empire that served as their foundation; they were themselves in contact with evolved empires that reacted back upon them; they actively prepared the way for new forms of the State (for example, absolute monarchy as the culmination of a certain kind of subjective law and a feudal process).45 In effect, in the rich domain of personal relations, what counts is not the capriciousness or variability of the individuals but the consistency of the relations, and the adequation between a subjectivity that can reach the point of delirium and qualified acts that are sources of rights and obligations. In a beautiful passage, Edgar Quinet underlines this coincidence between "the delirium of the twelve Cesars and the golden age of Roman law."46<br>The subjectifications, conjunctions, and appropriations do not prevent the decoded flows from continuing to flow, and from ceaselessly engendering new flows that escape (we saw this, for example, at the level of a micropolitics of the Middle Ages). This is where there is an ambiguity in these apparatuses: they can only function with decoded flows, and yet they do not let them stream together; they perform topical conjunctions that stand as so many knots or recodings. This accounts for the historians' impression that capitalism "could have" developed beginning at a certain moment, in China, in Rome, in Byzantium, in the Middle Ages, that the conditions for it existed but were not effectuated or even capable of being eff ectuated.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 And the question 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 de savoir si
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  these last formations still answer to the concept of State can only be 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pos\'e9e compte tenu de
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  certain correlations \cf3 \strokec3 [posed, account taken of \'97 poser + compte tenu (\'b631): the question admitted to the docket only with its ledger attached]\cf0 \strokec2 : quite as much as the evolved empires, the cities and the f\'e9odalit\'e9s suppose an archaic empire 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 qui leur sert de fond
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [that serves them as ground \'97 fond: the painter's ground, the backdrop: the Urstaat as the canvas under every later form]\cf0 \strokec2 ; they are themselves in contact with evolved empires that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 r\'e9agissent sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  them \cf3 \strokec3 [react back upon \'97 the \'b616 retroaction verb]\cf0 \strokec2 ; they actively prepare new forms of State (for example, absolute monarchy as 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 aboutissement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of a subjective droit and of a feudal process
\f5 \uc0\u8308 \u8304 
\f3  \cf3 \strokec3 [the end-point arrived at \'97 aboutir: the road's terminus: monarchy as where subjective law comes out]\cf0 \strokec2 ). In effect, in the rich domain of personal rapports, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ce qui compte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  is not the caprice or the variability of the persons, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 la consistance des rapports
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [what counts\'85 the consistency of the relations \'97 compter + consistance: the two chains joined: relations that hold, whatever the persons do]\cf0 \strokec2 , and the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ad\'e9quation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of a subjectivity that can go 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 jusqu'au d\'e9lire
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , with qualified acts that are sources of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 droits et d'obligations
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [adequation\'85 as far as delirium \'97 d\'e9lire: the Rhizome \'b64 word (the tree of delirium); obligations: ob-ligare, the bind-root (\'b69 fn.): even delirium yields bonds, provided the acts are qualified]\cf0 \strokec2 . In a beautiful page, Edgar Quinet underlined this coincidence between \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 le d\'e9lire des douze C\'e9sars et l'\'e2ge d'or du droit romain
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb
\f5 \uc0\u8308 
\f3 \'b9 \cf3 \strokec3 [the delirium of the twelve Caesars and the golden age of Roman law \'97 Quinet French-original, translated from the supplied French: mad subjects, perfect law \'97 the adequation's proof-case]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Or
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the subjectivations, the conjonctions, the appropriations 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 n'emp\'eachent pas les flux d\'e9cod\'e9s de continuer \'e0 couler
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [do not prevent the decoded flows from continuing to flow \'97 couler: the hydraulic chain, running free at last]\cf0 \strokec2 , and from 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 engendrer sans cesse
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  new flows that escape \cf3 \strokec3 [engendering ceaselessly \'97 the birth-chain's verb of generation]\cf0 \strokec2  (we have seen it for example, at the level of a micropolitics of the Middle Ages). It is even 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'\'e9quivoque
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of these apparatuses \cf3 \strokec3 [the equivocation \'97 \'e9quivoque: the double-speaking: apparatuses that say two things at once]\cf0 \strokec2 : at once they function only with decoded flows, and yet 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne les laissent pas concourir ensemble
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [do not let them run together \'97 concourir (\'b614, \'b629): the concourse prevented: the apparatus as anti-confluence device]\cf0 \strokec2 , operate the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 conjonctions topiques qui valent pour autant de n\'9cuds ou recodages
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [topical conjunctions that count as so many knots or recodings \'97 n\'9cuds: the \'b61 knots: the emperor's knot surviving in the evolved apparatus as the topical conjunction \'97 the conjonction IS the knot, the definition that makes \'b662's contrast cut]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 D'o\'f9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the impression of the historians when they say that capitalism \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 aurait pu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb se produire from that moment on \cf3 \strokec3 [\'ab could have \'bb \'97 the conditional itself in scare-quotes: the counterfactual held with tweezers, the historians' mood exhibited as specimen]\cf0 \strokec2  \'97 in China, at Rome, at Byzantium, in the Middle Ages \'97 that the conditions were 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 donn\'e9es
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , but were not 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 effectu\'e9es ni m\'eame effectuables
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [given\'85 neither effectuated nor even effectuatable \'97 donn\'e9es (\'b610) + the -able suffix: the virtual/actual machinery: conditions present, actualization not even possible]\cf0 \strokec2 .\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

