\f6 \cf2 \'b662 fr.563 umn.452
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 C'est que la pression des flux dessine en creux le capitalisme, mais qu'il faut pour le r\'e9aliser toute une int\'e9grale des flux d\'e9cod\'e9s, toute une conjugaison g\'e9n\'e9ralis\'e9e qui d\'e9borde et renverse les appareils pr\'e9c\'e9dents . Et en effet, quand il s'agit pour Marx de d\'e9finir le capitalisme, il commence par invoquer l'av\'e8nement d'une seule Subjectivit\'e9 globale et non qualifi\'e9e, qui capitalise tous les processus de subjectivation, \'ab toutes les activit\'e9s sans distinction \'bb : \'ab l'activit\'e9 productrice en g\'e9n\'e9ral \'bb, \'ab l'essence subjective unique de la richesse . . . \'bb. Et ce Sujet unique s'exprime maintenant dans un Objet quelconque, non plus dans tel ou tel \'e9tat qualitatif : \'ab Avec l 'universalit\'e9 abstraite de l'activit\'e9 cr\'e9atrice de richesse, on a en m\'eame temps l'universalit\'e9 de l'objet en tant que richesse, le produit tout court ou le travail tout court, mais, en tant que travail pass\'e9, mat\'e9rialis\'e9 41 . \'bb La circulation constitue le capital comme subjectivit\'e9 ad\'e9quate \'e0 la soci\'e9t\'e9 tout enti\'e8re.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 The situation is that the pressure of the flows draws capitalism in negative outline, but for it to be realized there must be a whole integral of decoded flows, a whole generalized conjunction that overspills and overturns the preceding apparatuses. And in fact when Marx sets about defining capitalism, he begins by invoking the advent of a single unqualified and global Subjectivity, which capitalizes all of the processes of subjectification, "all activities without distinction": "productive activity in general," "the sole subjective essence of wealth . . . " And this single Subject now expresses itself in an Object in general, no longer in this or that qualitative state: "Along with the abstract universality of wealth-creating activity we have now the universality of the object defined as wealth, viz. the product in general, or labor in general, but as past, materialized labor."47 Circulation constitutes capital as a subjectivity commensurate with society in its entirety.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f7 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u9888 
\f3  QUOTATION FLAG \'97 Marx, Introduction g\'e9n\'e9rale (Grundrisse introduction; fn. 42). German original via Pl\'e9iade; Massumi's "viz. the product in general, or labor in general, but as past, materialized labor" has the cadence of the published English \'97 restoration pattern. Verified English Grundrisse introduction requested before flags against the quotation.\
It is that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 la pression des flux dessine en creux le capitalisme
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the pressure of the flows draws capitalism en creux \'97 in hollow: the intaglio and the mold: capitalism as negative relief, the shape pressed into what resists it]\cf0 \strokec2 , but that to realize it there must be 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 toute une int\'e9grale des flux d\'e9cod\'e9s
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [a whole integral of the decoded flows \'97 int\'e9grale: the calculus integral: the flows summed under one sign]\cf0 \strokec2 , 
