\f6 \cf2 \'b666 fr.566 umn.453
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Car l 'Etat, d\'e8s le pal\'e9olithique ou le n\'e9olithique, est d\'e9territorialisant dans la mesure o\'f9 il fait de la terre un objet de son unit\'e9 sup\'e9rieure, un ensemble forc\'e9 de coexistence au lieu du libre jeu des territoires entre eux et avec les lignages . Mais c'est pr\'e9cis\'e9ment en ce sens que l'Etat est dit \'ab territorial \'bb . Tandis que l e capitalisme n'est pas d u tout territorial, m\'eame \'e0 ses d\'e9buts : sa puissance de d\'e9territorialisation consiste \'e0 prendre pour objet, non pas m\'eame la terre, mais le \'ab travail mat\'e9rialis\'e9 \'bb, la marchandise. Et la propri\'e9t\'e9 priv\'e9e n'est plus celle de la terre ou du sol, ni m\'eame de moyens de production comme tels, mais celle de droits abstraits convertibles 47. C'est pourquoi le capitalisme marque une mutation des organisations \'9ccum\'e9niques ou mondiales, qui prennent une consistance en elles-m\'eames : au lieu de r\'e9sulter des formations sociales h\'e9t\'e9rog\'e8nes et de leurs rapports, c'est l'axiomatique mondiale en grande partie qui distribue ces formations, fixe leurs rapports, en organisant une division internationale du travail. Sous tous ces aspects, on dirait que le capitalisme d\'e9veloppe un ordre \'e9conomique qui pourrait se passer d'Etat. Et en effet le capitalisme ne manque pas de cris de guerre contre l'Etat, non seulement au nom du march\'e9, mais en vertu de sa d\'e9territorialisation sup\'e9rieure.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 For since Paleolithic and Neolithic times, the State has been deterritorializing to the extent that it makes the earth an ob ject of its higher unity, a forced aggregate of coexistence, instead ofthe free play of territories among themselves and with the lineages. But this is precisely the sense in which the State is termed "territorial." Capitalism, on the other hand, is not at all territorial, even in its beginnings: its power of deterritorialization consists in taking as its object, not the earth, but "materialized labor," the commodity. And private property is no longer ownership of the land or the soil, nor even of the means of production as such, but of convertible abstract rights. 53 That is why capitalism marks a mutation in worldwide or ecumenical organizations, which now take on a consistency of their own: the worldwide axiomatic, instead of resulting from heterogeneous social formations and their relations, for the most part distributes these formations, determines their relations, while organizing an international division of labor. From all these standpoints, it could be said that capitalism develops an economic order that could do without the State. And in fact capitalism is not short on war cries against the State, not only in the name of the market, but by virtue of its superior deterritorialization.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For the State, from the Paleolithic or the Neolithic, is deterritorializing 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 dans la mesure o\'f9 il fait de la terre un objet de son unit\'e9 sup\'e9rieure
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [in the measure that it makes of the earth an object of its superior unity \'97 the faire de X un Y signature (\'b62, \'b611) + the \'b620 formula (territory pris comme objet): the State's founding operation restated]\cf0 \strokec2 , a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 forced ensemble of coexistence
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  in place of the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 libre jeu
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the territories among themselves and with the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 lignages
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [free play \'97 jeu: the play of parts, mechanical slack and game both (\'b623 jouent); lineages \'97 the \'b68 codes lignagers: the lineage-register kept]\cf0 \strokec2 . But it is precisely in this sense that the State is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 dit \'ab territorial \'bb
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [called \'ab territorial \'bb \'97 the paradox in scare-quotes: named for what it destroys \'97 territorial because it deterritorializes the territories into land]\cf0 \strokec2 . Whereas capitalism is not at all territorial, even at its 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e9buts
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 : its power of deterritorialization consists in taking for object, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 non pas m\'eame la terre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , but \'ab materialized labor \'bb, the merchandise \cf3 \strokec3 [not even the earth \'97 the escalation: the State took the earth from the territories; capital takes not-even-the-earth \'97 one rung further from ground]\cf0 \strokec2 . And private property is no longer that of the earth or the soil, nor even of means of production 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 comme tels
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , but that of convertible abstract 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 droits
\f5\i0\b0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8308 \u8311 
\f3 . That is why capitalism marks a mutation of the ecumenical or worldwide organizations, which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 prennent une consistance en elles-m\'eames
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [take on a consistency in themselves \'97 the prendre consistance idiom (\'b617, \'b621, \'b626): the world-organization finally setting]\cf0 \strokec2 : instead of resulting from the heterogeneous social formations and their rapports, it is the worldwide axiomatic in large part that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 distribue
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  these formations, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fixe
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  their rapports \cf3 \strokec3 [distributes\'85 fixes \'97 the \'b624 relation inverted: the ecumenical order no longer the formations' product but their distributor; fixer (\'b614, \'b638): the pinning verb]\cf0 \strokec2 , while organizing an international division of labor. Under all these aspects, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 on dirait que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  capitalism develops an economic order that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pourrait se passer d'\'c9tat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one would say that \'97 the hedged-appearance formula (\'b612); could do without the State \'97 se passer de: the by-pass, primed for \'b668's pun]\cf0 \strokec2 . And in effect capitalism 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne manque pas de cris de guerre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  against the State \cf3 \strokec3 [does not lack war cries \'97 manquer + the war register: capital's own bellicosity, borrowed from the machine it captured]\cf0 \strokec2 , not only in the name of the market, but 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 en vertu de
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  its superior deterritorialization.\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

