\f6 \cf2 \'b670 fr.568 umn.455
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Mais, d'autre part et surtout, parce que les Etats socialistes bureaucratiques peuvent eux-m\'eames d\'e9velopper des rapports de production diff\'e9rents, qui ne se conjuguent avec le capitalisme que pour former un ensemble dont la \'ab puissance \'bb d\'e9borde l'axiomatique elle-m\'eame ( il faudra essayer de d\'e9terminer la nature de cette puissance, pourquoi nous la pensons si souvent de mani\'e8re apocalyptique, quels conflits elle engendre, quelles chances incertaines elle nous laisse . . . ). - 3 ) Une typologie des Etats modernes rejoindrait ainsi une m\'e9ta-\'e9conomie : il serait inexact de traiter tous les Etats comme \'ab se valant \'bb ( m\'eame l'isomorphie n'a pas cette cons\'e9quence) ; mais non moins inexact de privil\'e9gier telle forme d'Etat (en oubliant que la polymorphie \'e9tablit de strictes compl\'e9mentarit\'e9s, par exemple entre les d\'e9mocraties occidentales et les tyrannies coloniales ou n\'e9ocoloniales qu'elles instaurent ou entretiennent ailleurs) ; non moins inexact e1'lcore d'assimiler les Etats socialistes bureaucratiques \'e0 des Etats capitalistes totalitaires ( en n\'e9gligeant que l'axiomatique peut 48. Les livres d'introduction \'e0 la m\'e9thode axiomatique soulignent un certain nombre de probl\'e8mes. Soit le beau livre de Robert Blanch\'e9, L'axiomatique, P. U. F. Il y a d'abord la question de l'ind\'e9pendance respective des axiomes, et de la saturation ou non du syst\'e8me ( \'a7\'a7 14 et 15). En second lieu, les \'ab mod\'e8les de r\'e9alisation \'bb, leur h\'e9t\'e9rog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9, mais aussi leur isomorphie par rapport \'e0 l'axiomatique (\'a7 12). Et puis l'\'e9ventuali\'e9 d'une polymorphie des mod\'e8les, non seulement dans un syst\'e8me non satur\'e9, mais m\'eame dans une axiomatique satur\'e9e ( \'a7\'a7 12, 15, 26). Et puis, encore, la question des \'ab propositions ind\'e9cidables \'bb auxquelles se heurte une axIomatique (\'a7 20).
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 But on the other hand, and this is the main point, the bureaucratic socialist States can themselves develop different modes of production that only conjugate with capitalism to form a set whose "power" exceeds that of the axiomatic itself (it will be necessary to try to determine the nature of this power, why we so often think of it in apocalyptic terms, what conflicts it spawns, what slim chances it leaves us . . . ).<br>3. A typology of modern States is thus coupled with a metaeconomics: it would be inaccurate to treat all States as "interchangeable" (even isomorphy does not have that consequence), but it would be no less inaccurate to privilege a certain form of the State (forgetting that polymorphy establishes strict complementarities between the Western democracies and the colonial or neocolonial tyrannies that they install or support in other regions) or to equate the bureaucratic socialist States with the totalitarian capitalist States (neglecting the fact that the axiomatic can encompass a real heteromorphy from which the higher power of the aggregate derives, even if it is for the worse).
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 But, on the other hand and above all, because the bureaucratic socialist States can themselves develop different 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rapports de production
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [relations of production \'97 the Marxist term of art, deliberately alternated with \'b669's modes de production: relations, not modes \'97 see flag 1]\cf0 \strokec2 , which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne se conjuguent avec le capitalisme que pour former un ensemble dont la \'ab puissance \'bb d\'e9borde l'axiomatique elle-m\'eame
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [conjugate with capitalism only to form a set whose \'ab power \'bb overflows the axiomatic itself \'97 se conjuguer (\'b663); \'ab puissance \'bb scare-quoted: the mathematician's power, the cardinality of a set (fn. 48's puissance du continu): the socialist-capitalist ensemble as a set of higher cardinality than its axiomatic \'97 Cantor in geopolitics; d\'e9border: the flood again]\cf0 \strokec2  (
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il faudra essayer de d\'e9terminer
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the nature of this puissance, why we think it so often 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 de mani\'e8re apocalyptique
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , what conflicts it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 engendre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , what 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 chances incertaines
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  it leaves us\'85 \cf3 \strokec3 [it will be necessary to try \'97 the forward-promise voice; uncertain chances \'97 incertain: of unknown magnitude, not small: the future left open, not rationed]\cf0 \strokec2 ). \'97 3) A typology of modern States 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 rejoindrait ainsi une m\'e9ta-\'e9conomie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [would thus rejoin a meta-economics \'97 conditional + rejoindre: the catch-up verb (\'b623, \'b663): typology running to meet economics]\cf0 \strokec2 : 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 il serait inexact de traiter
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  all States as \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se valant
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb \cf3 \strokec3 [it would be inexact to treat all States as \'ab being worth one another \'bb \'97 the valoir chain (\'b65, \'b614) reflexive-reciprocal, scare-quoted: equivalence as mutual worth, not substitutability]\cf0 \strokec2  (even isomorphy does not have this consequence); but no less inexact to privilege 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 telle forme d'\'c9tat
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  (forgetting that polymorphy establishes strict 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 compl\'e9mentarit\'e9s
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , for example between the Western democracies and the colonial or neocolonial tyrannies that they 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 instaurent ou entretiennent ailleurs
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [install or keep up elsewhere \'97 entretenir (\'b610, \'b613, \'b626): the provisioning verb: democracies as the tyrannies' housekeepers, upkeep not mere support]\cf0 \strokec2 ); no less inexact again to assimilate the bureaucratic socialist States to totalitarian capitalist States (neglecting that the axiomatic can 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 comporter
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  a real heteromorphy 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 dont se d\'e9gage la puissance d'ensemble sup\'e9rieure, m\'eame si c'est pour le pire
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [from which the superior power-of-the-set extracts itself, even if it is for the worse \'97 se d\'e9gager + puissance d'ensemble: cardinality again; pour le pire: the marriage-vow half (\'b63, le meilleur et le pire) at its last appearance \'97 the world-set wedded for worse]\cf0 \strokec2 ).\

\f5 \uc0\u8308 \u8312 
\f3  The books of introduction to the axiomatic method underline a certain number of problems. Take the beautiful book of Robert Blanch\'e9, \ul \strokec2 L'axiomatique\ulnone \strokec2 , P.U.F. There is first the question of the respective independence of the axioms, and of the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 saturation
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  or not of the system (\'a7\'a7 14\'9615). In second place, the \'ab models of realization \'bb, their heterogeneity, but also their isomorphy in relation to the axiomatic (\'a7 12). And then the eventuality of a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 polymorphy
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the models, not only in a non-saturated system, but even in a saturated axiomatic (\'a7\'a7 12, 15, 26). And then, again, the question of the \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 propositions ind\'e9cidables
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb against which an axiomatic runs up (\'a7 20) \cf3 \strokec3 [undecidable propositions \'97 the G\'f6delian register entering the plateau's toolkit, held in reserve for the axiomatics proposition]\cf0 \strokec2 . \cf3 \strokec3 (fn. 48 continues into \'b671's cell; French 48 = Minnesota 54)\cf0 \strokec2 \
