\f6 \cf2 \'b672 fr.569 umn.456
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 C'est sur ces flux d\'e9cod\'e9s et d\'e9territorialis\'e9s que la nation se constitue, et ne se s\'e9pare pas de l'Etat moderne qui donne une consistance \'e0 la terre et au peuple correspondants. C'est le flux de travail nu qui fait le peuple, comme c'est le flux de Capital qui fait la terre et son \'e9quipement. Bref, la nation est l'op\'e9ration m\'eame d'une subjectivation collective, auquel l 'Etat moderne correspond comme proc\'e8s d'assujettissement. C'est bien sous cette forme d'Etat-nation, avec toutes les diversit\'e9s possibles, que l'Etat devient mod\'e8le de r\'e9alisation pour l'axiomatique capitaliste. Ce qui ne revient nullement \'e0 dire que les nations soient des apparences ou des ph\'e9nom\'e8nes id\'e9ologiques, mais au contraire les formes vivantes et passionnelles o\'f9 se r\'e9alisent d'abord l'homog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9 qualitative et la concurrence quantitative du capital abstrait. Nous distinguons comme deux concepts l'asservissement machinique et l'assujettissement social. Il y a asservissement lorsque les hommes sont eux-m\'eames pi\'e8ces constituantes d'une machine, qu'ils composent entre eux et avec d'autres choses (b\'eates, outils), sous le contr\'f4le et la direction d'une unit\'e9 sup\'e9rieure. Mais il y a assujettissement lorsque l'unit\'e9 sup\'e9rieure constitue l'homme comme un sujet qui se rapporte \'e0 un objet devenu ext\'e9rieur, que cet objet soit lui-m\'eame une b\'eate, un outil ou m\'eame une machine : l'homme alors n'est plus composante de la machine, mais ouvrier, 5 70 APP AREIL DE CAPTURE usager . . . , il est assujetti \'e0 la machine, et non plus asservi par la machine. Ce n'est pas dire que le second r\'e9gime est plus humain.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 The nation is constituted on the basis of these flows and is inseparable from the modern State that gives consistency to the corresponding land and people. It is the flow of naked labor that makes the people, just as it is the flow of Capital that makes the land and its industrial base. In short, the nation is the very operation of a collective subjectification, to which the modern State corresponds as a process of subjection. It is in the form ofthe nation-state, with all its possible variations, that the State becomes the model of realization for the capitalist axiomatic. This is not at all to say that nations are appearances or ideological phenomena; on the contrary, they are the passional and living forms in which the qualitative homogeneity and the quantitative competition of abstract capital are first realized.<br>We distinguish machinic enslavement and social sub jection as two separate concepts. There is enslavement when human beings themselves are 7000 R.C.: APPARA TUS OF CAPTURE 0 457 constituent pieces of a machine that they compose among themselves and with other things (animals, tools), under the control and direction of a higher unity. But there is subjection when the higher unity constitutes the human being as a subject linked to a now exterior object, which can be an animal, a tool, or even a machine. The human being is no longer a component of the machine but a worker, a user. He or she is subjected to the machine and no longer enslaved by the machine. This is not to say that the second regime is more human.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It is on these 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 flux d\'e9cod\'e9s et d\'e9territorialis\'e9s
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  that the nation constitutes itself \cf3 \strokec3 [decoded and deterritorialized flows \'97 both adjectives load-bearing: the nation built on precisely the flows the old forms lost]\cf0 \strokec2 , and it does not separate itself from the modern State that gives a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 consistance
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  to the corresponding land and people. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 C'est le flux de travail nu qui fait le peuple, comme c'est le flux de Capital qui fait la terre et son \'e9quipement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [it is the flow of naked labor that makes the people, as it is the flow of Capital that makes the land and its equipment \'97 the double cleft: two flows, two makings; \'e9quipement (\'b667): the outfitting, wider than industry; Capital capitalized against travail nu lowercase]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Bref
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , the nation is the very operation of a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 subjectivation collective
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , to which the modern State corresponds as 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 proc\'e8s d'assujettissement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [process of subjection \'97 the \'b659 pair distributed: nation subjectifies, State subjects]\cf0 \strokec2 . It is indeed under this form of \'c9tat-nation, with all possible diversities, that the State becomes model of realization for the capitalist axiomatic. 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ce qui ne revient nullement \'e0 dire que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the nations are appearances or ideological phenomena \cf3 \strokec3 [which does not at all come back to saying \'97 revenir (\'b69): the inference refused in the return-idiom]\cf0 \strokec2 , but on the contrary the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 formes vivantes et passionnelles
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  where 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 se r\'e9alisent d'abord l'homog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9 qualitative et la concurrence quantitative du capital abstrait
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the living and passional forms where the qualitative homogeneity and the quantitative competition of abstract capital first realize themselves \'97 concurrence (\'b668): con-currere as noun; the qualitative/quantitative pair recycling \'b667's Sweezy formula: nations as where the formula becomes flesh]\cf0 \strokec2 . We distinguish as two concepts 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'asservissement machinique
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  and 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 l'assujettissement social
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . There is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 asservissement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  when men are themselves 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 pi\'e8ces constituantes
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of a machine \cf3 \strokec3 [constituent pieces \'97 pi\'e8ce: the machine-part and the chess-piece: men as components]\cf0 \strokec2 , which they compose among themselves and with other things (beasts, tools), under the control and direction of a superior unity. But there is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 assujettissement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  when the superior unity constitutes man as a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 sujet qui se rapporte \'e0 un objet devenu ext\'e9rieur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [a subject who relates himself to an object become exterior \'97 se rapporter (\'b66): the referral-verb at subjection's very definition: the subject IS the one who refers to an outside \'97 subjecthood as rapport]\cf0 \strokec2 , whether this object be itself a beast, a tool or even a machine: man then is no longer a component of the machine, but worker, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 usager
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 \'85 \cf3 \strokec3 [user \'97 usage: the \'b69/\'b633 register (pr\'eat d'usage, valeur d'usage): the user as the machine's usufructuary]\cf0 \strokec2 , he is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 assujetti \'e0
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the machine, and no longer 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 asservi par
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the machine \cf3 \strokec3 [subjected TO\'85 enslaved BY \'97 the \'e0/par pair: two prepositions carrying the two regimes: relation to an exterior vs. incorporation by an interior]\cf0 \strokec2 . This is not to say that the second regime is more human.\cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 \cell \row

