\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , and as the cadre 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'\'e9tend \'e0 la soci\'e9t\'e9 tout enti\'e8re
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [extends itself to the whole society \'97 the \'b662 measure (capital adequate to the whole society) fulfilled]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 On dirait aussi bien qu'un peu de subjectivation nous \'e9loignait de l'asservissement machinique, mais que beaucoup nous y ram\'e8ne
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [one would say just as well that a little subjectivation took us away from machinic enslavement, but that a lot brings us back to it \'97 the dosage aphorism: subjectivation as homeopathic in small doses, toxic at scale; ramener (\'b64, \'b668): the bringing-back verb]\cf0 \strokec2 . One has recently underlined 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e0 quel point
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the exercise of modern power 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne se r\'e9duisait pas
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  to the classical alternative \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 r\'e9pression ou id\'e9ologie
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb \cf3 \strokec3 [the Foucault allusion: power irreducible to the repression/ideology pair]\cf0 \strokec2 , but implied processes of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 normalisation, de modulation, de mod\'e9lisation, d'information
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [normalization, modulation, modeling, information \'97 the -ation series: the control-society vocabulary arriving early, modulation as its keyword]\cf0 \strokec2 , which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 portent sur
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  language, perception, desire, movement, etc., and which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 passent par des micro-agencements
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 .\

\f5 \uc0\u8309 \u8304 
\f3  Ergonomics distinguishes \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 homme-machine
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb systems (work stations) and \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 hommes-machines
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb systems (communicating ensembles of human and non-human elements) \cf3 \strokec3 [the singular/plural distinction: one man at one machine vs. plural elements in one circuit \'97 the conceptual weight carried entirely by two letters s]\cf0 \strokec2 . And it is not only a difference of degree, the second point of view is not a generalization of the first: \'ab The notion of information loses its anthropocentric aspect \'bb, and the problems are not of adaptation, but of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 choix d'un \'e9l\'e9ment humain ou non humain suivant le cas
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . Cf. Maurice de Montmollin, \ul \strokec2 Les syst\'e8mes hommes-machines\ulnone \strokec2 , P.U.F. The question is no longer to adapt, even under violence, but to localize: 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 o\'f9 est ta place ?
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [where is your place? \'97 the familiar tu: the system addressing you in the singular, intimate and assigning]\cf0 \strokec2  Even 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 les infirmit\'e9s
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  can serve, instead of being corrected or compensated \cf3 \strokec3 [the infirmities \'97 the \'b63\'964 arc's cybernetic terminus: the State that needed the born-infirm (Borgne, Manchot, mutil\'e9s pr\'e9existants) now finds infirmity USEFUL as such \'97 the plateau's darkest rhyme]\cf0 \strokec2 . A deaf-mute can be essential in a \'ab hommes-machines \'bb communication system.\
