\f5 \uc0\u8309 \u8309 
\f3  The \'ab intuitionist \'bb school (Brouwer, Heyting, Griss, Bouligand, etc.) has a great mathematical importance, not because it 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 a fait valoir
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  irreducible rights of intuition \cf3 \strokec3 [asserted, made prevail \'97 faire valoir (\'b678): the claim-idiom]\cf0 \strokec2 , nor even because it elaborated a very new constructionism, but because it develops a conception of problems, and of a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 calcul des probl\'e8mes
