\f6 \cf2 Car il co\'efncide avec le p\'f4le totalitaire par l'\'e9crasement du march\'e9 int\'e9rieur et la r\'e9duction des axiomes . Cependant, la promotion du secteur externe ne se fait pas du tout par appel aux capitaux ext\'e9rieurs et industrie d'exportation, mais par \'e9conomie de guerre, qui entra\'eene un expansionnisme \'e9tranger au totalitarisme et une fabrication autonome de capital. Quant au march\'e9 int\'e9rieur, il est effectu\'e9 par une production sp\'e9cifique d'Ersatz. Si bien que le fascisme comporte aussi une prolif\'e9ration d'axiomes, qui fait qu'on l'a souvent rapproch\'e9 d'une \'e9conomie keyn\'e9sienne. Seulement, c'est une prolif\'e9ration fictive ou tautologique, un multiolicateur par soustraction, qui fait du fascisme un cas tr\'e8s sp\'e9cial 56 . 2 . Saturation. - Peut-on distribuer les deux tendances inverses en disant que la saturation du syst\'e8me marque le point d'inversion ? Non, car c'est plut\'f4t la saturation qui est elle-m\'eame relative. Si Marx a montr\'e9 le fonctionnement du capitalisme comme une axiomatique, c'est surtout dans le chapitre c\'e9l\'e8bre sur la baisse
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 It coincides with the totalitarian pole in the collapse of the domestic market and the reduction in the number of axioms. However, the promotion of the foreign sector does not at all take place through an appeal to foreign sources of capital and through export industries, but through a war economy, which entails an expansionism foreign to totalitarianism and an autonomous fabrication of capital. As for the domestic market, it is eff ectuated in a specific production of the Ersatz. This means that fascism, too, brings a proliferation ofaxioms, which explains why it has of ten been compared to a Keynesian economy. Fascism, however, is a tautological or fictitious prolif eration, a multiplication by subtraction; this makes it a very special case.62<br>2. Saturation. Can we express the distribution of the two opposite tendencies by saying that the saturation of the system marks the point of inversion? No, for the saturation is itself relative. If Marx demonstrated the functioning of capitalism as an axiomatic, it was above all in the famous chapter on the tendency of the rate of profit to fall.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For it coincides with the totalitarian pole by the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9crasement
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  of the interior market and the reduction of the axioms \cf3 \strokec3 [crushing \'97 \'e9craser (\'b671, the nations crushing their minorities): active, agented \'97 fascism CRUSHES the domestic market, where totalitarianism's market s'effondre, caves in (\'b684): two verbs, two poles, one active one intransitive]\cf0 \strokec2 . However, the promotion of the external sector 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne se fait pas du tout
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  by appeal to exterior capitals and export industry, but by 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9conomie de guerre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [war economy \'97 the guerre chain in its fiscal uniform]\cf0 \strokec2 , which 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 entra\'eene
