\f4\i\b \strokec2 \'e9tranger au totalitarisme
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [carries along an expansionism foreign to totalitarianism \'97 \'e9tranger: the pun quietly working \'97 no foreign capital, but an expansionism foreign-to]\cf0 \strokec2  and an autonomous fabrication of capital. As for the interior market, it is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 effectu\'e9
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  by a specific production of 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Ersatz
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [Ersatz \'97 the German kept: the substitute-goods economy named in the regime's own language]\cf0 \strokec2 . So that fascism 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 comporte
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  also a proliferation of axioms, 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 qui fait qu'on l'a souvent rapproch\'e9 d'une
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  Keynesian economy. Only, it is a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 fictive or tautological proliferation, un multiplicateur par soustraction
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [a multiplier by subtraction \'97 the arithmetic oxymoron: fascism's Keynesianism as a times-sign built from a minus]\cf0 \strokec2 , which 
