\f6 \cf2 \'b688 fr.578 umn.463
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 Il y a toujours une diff\'e9rence fondamentale entre les flux vivants et les axiomes qui les subordonnent \'e0 des centres de contr\'f4le et de d\'e9cision, qui leur font correspondre tel ou tel segment, qui en mesurent les quanta. Mais la pression des flux vivants, et des probl\'e8mes qu'ils posent et imposent, doit s'exercer \'e0 l'int\'e9rieur de l'axiomatique, aussi bien pour lutter contre les r\'e9ductions totalitaires que pour devancer et pr\'e9cipiter les adjonctions, les orienter, et en emp\'eacher la perversion technocratique. 3. Mod\'e8les\} isomorphie. - En principe, tous les Etats sont isomorphes, c'est-\'e0-dire sont des domaines de r\'e9alisation du capital en fonction d'un seul et m\'eame march\'e9 mondial ext\'e9rieur. Mais une premi\'e8re question serait de savoir si l'isomorphie implique une homog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9 ou m\'eame une homog\'e9n\'e9isation des Etats. Oui, comme on le voit dans l'Europe actuelle, concernant la justice et la police, le code routier, la circulation des marchandises, les co\'fbts de production, etc. Mais ce n'est vrai que dans la mesure o\'f9 il y a tendance \'e0 un march\'e9 int\'e9rieur unique int\'e9gr\'e9 . Sinon, l 'isomorphisme n 'implique nullement l'homog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9 : il y a isomorphie, mais h\'e9t\'e9rog\'e9n\'e9it\'e9, entre Etats totalitaires et sociaux-d\'e9mocrates, chaque fois que le mode de production est le m\'eame. Les r\'e8gles g\'e9n\'e9rales \'e0 cet \'e9gard sont les suivantes : la consistance, l'ensemble ou l)unit\'e9 de l\}axiomatique sont d\'e9finis par le capital comme \'ab droit \'bb ou rapport de production (pour le march\'e9) ; l'ind\'e9pendance respective des axiomes ne contredit nullement cet ensemble, mais vient des divisions et secteurs du mode de production capitaliste ; l'isomorphie des mod\'e8les, avec les deux p\'f4les d'adjonction et de soustraction, revient \'e0 la distribution dans chaque cas du march\'e9 int\'e9rieur et du march\'e9 ext\'e9rieur.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 There is always a fundamental difference between Ii ving flows and the axioms that subordinate them to centers of control and decision making, that make a given segment correspond to them, which measure their quanta. But the pressure of the living flows, and of the problems they pose and impose, must be exerted inside the axiomatic, as much in order to fight the totalitarian reductions as to anticipate and precipitate the additions, to orient them and prevent their technocratic perversion.<br>3. Models, isomorphie. In principle, all States are isomorphic; in other words, they are domains of realization of capital as a function of a sole external world market. But the first question is whether isomorphy implies a homogeneity or even a homogenization of States. The answer is yes, as can be seen in present-day Europe with respect to justice and the police, the highway code, the circulation of commodities, production costs, etc. But this is true only insofar as there is a tendency toward a single integrated domestic market. Otherwise, isomorphy in no way implies homogeneity: there is isomorphy, but heterogeneity, between totalitarian and social democratic States wherever the mode of production is the same. The general rules regarding this are as follows: the consistency, the totality (l 'ensemble), or unity of the axiomatic are defined by capital as a "right" or relation of production (for the market); the respective independence of the axioms in no way contradicts this totality but derives from the divisions or sectors of the capitalist mode of production; the isomorphy of the models, with the two poles of addition and subtraction, depends on how the domestic and foreign markets are distributed in each case.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 There is always a fundamental difference between the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 flux vivants
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  and the axioms that subordinate them to centers of control and decision, that 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 leur font correspondre tel ou tel segment
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [make such-and-such a segment correspond to them \'97 the faire-correspondre causative (\'b638): correspondence manufactured]\cf0 \strokec2 , that measure their 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 quanta
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [quanta \'97 the physics plural: flows metered in discrete packets]\cf0 \strokec2 . But the pressure of the living flows, and of the problems they 
