\f6 \cf2 Ce qui d\'e9finit donc une minorit\'e9, ce n'est pas le nombre, ce sont les rapports int\'e9rieurs au nombre. Une minorit\'e9 peut \'eatre nombreuse ou m\'eame infinie ; de m\'eame une majorit\'e9. Ce qui les distingue, c'est que le rapport int\'e9rieur au nombre constitue dans le cas d'une majorit\'e9 un ensemble, fini ou infini, mais toujours d\'e9nombrable, tandis que la minorit\'e9 se d\'e9finit comme ensemble non d\'e9nombrable, quel que soit le nombre de ses \'e9l\'e9ments. Ce qui caract\'e9rise l'ind\'e9nombrable, ce n'est ni l'ensemble ni les \'e9l\'e9ments ; c'est plut\'f4t la connexion, le \'ab et \'bb, qui se produit entre les \'e9l\'e9ments, entre les ensembles, et qui n'appartient \'e0 aucun des deux, qui leur \'e9chappe et constitue une ligne de fuite. Or l'axiomatique ne manie que des ensembles d\'e9nombrables, m\'eame infinis, tandis que les minorit\'e9s constituent ces ensembles \'ab flous \'bb non d\'e9nombrables, non axiomatisables, bref ces \'ab masses \'bb, ces multiplicit\'e9s de fuite ou de flux. - Que ce soit l'ensemble infini des non-blancs de la p\'e9riph\'e9rie, ou l'ensemble r\'e9duit des Basques, des Corses, etc., nous voyons partout les pr\'e9misses d'un mouvement mondial : les minorit\'e9s recr\'e9ent des ph\'e9nom\'e8nes \'ab nationalitaires \'bb que les Etats-nations s'\'e9taient charg\'e9s de contr\'f4ler et d'\'e9touffer.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6 \cf2 What defines a minority, then, is not the number but the relations internal to the number. A minority can be numerous, or even infinite; so can a majority. What distinguishes them is that in the case of a majority the relation internal to the number constitutes a set that may be finite or infinite, but is always denumerable, whereas the minority is defined as a nondenumerable set, however many elements it may have. What characterizes the non denumerable is neither the set nor its elements; rather, it is the connection, the "and" produced between elements, between sets, and which belongs to neither, which eludes them and constitutes a line of flight. The axiomatic manipulates only denumerable sets, even infinite ones, whereas the minorities constitute "fuzzy," nondenumerable, nonaxiomizable sets, in short, "masses," multiplicities of escape and flux.<br>Whether it be the infinite set of the nonwhites of the periphery, or the restricted set of the Basques, Corsicans, etc., everywhere we look we see the conditions for a worldwide movement: the minorities recreate "nationalitarian" phenomena that the nation-states had been charged with controlling and quashing.
\f1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What defines a minority, then, is not the number, it is 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 les rapports int\'e9rieurs au nombre
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the relations interior to the number \'97 rapport again: number as a bundle of internal relations, not a count]\cf0 \strokec2 . A minority can be numerous or even infinite; likewise a majority. What distinguishes them is that the relation interior to the number constitutes, in the case of a majority, an 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ensemble
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , finite or infinite, but always 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 d\'e9nombrable
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , whereas the minority defines itself as 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ensemble non d\'e9nombrable
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , whatever the number of its elements \cf3 \strokec3 [denumerable/nondenumerable \'97 Cantor's distinction (fn. 48's puissance du continu) cashed as political ontology: majority counts, minority has the cardinality of the continuum]\cf0 \strokec2 . What characterizes the 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ind\'e9nombrable
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  is neither the ensemble nor the elements; it is rather 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 la connexion, le \'ab et \'bb
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 , which produces itself between the elements, between the ensembles, and which belongs to neither of the two, which escapes them and constitutes a 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ligne de fuite
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the connection, the \'ab and \'bb \'97 connexion: the \'b678 triple's first term (connexion / conjonction / conjugaison) finally defined, and it is Rhizome's own ET (\'85and\'85and\'85and\'85): the minority's operation is the rhizomatic conjunction itself \'97 the two books' vocabularies fusing in one clause]\cf0 \strokec2 . 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 Or
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  the axiomatic 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 ne manie que
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  denumerable ensembles, even infinite ones \cf3 \strokec3 [handles only \'97 manier: the hand-verb (\'b687 remaniements): the axiomatic's manual grip]\cf0 \strokec2 , whereas the minorities constitute those \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 flous
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb, nondenumerable, non-axiomatizable ensembles \cf3 \strokec3 [\'ab fuzzy \'bb sets \'97 ensembles flous: the technical term (Zadeh's fuzzy sets, standardly ensembles flous in French): the mathematics of vague membership borrowed live, scare-quoted as a citation from the discipline]\cf0 \strokec2 , in short those \'ab masses \'bb, those 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 multiplicit\'e9s de fuite ou de flux
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2 . \'97 Whether it be the infinite ensemble of the non-whites of the periphery, or the reduced ensemble of the Basques, the Corsicans, etc., we see everywhere 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 les pr\'e9misses d'un mouvement mondial
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [the premises of a worldwide movement \'97 pr\'e9misse: the syllogism's premise: the movement already entailed, awaiting only its conclusion]\cf0 \strokec2 : the minorities recreate \'ab 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 nationalitaires
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \'bb phenomena that the nation-States 
\f4\i\b \strokec2 s'\'e9taient charg\'e9s de contr\'f4ler et d'\'e9touffer
\f3\i0\b0 \strokec2  \cf3 \strokec3 [had charged themselves with controlling and smothering \'97 se charger (\'b687) + \'e9touffer: the suffocation verb: phenomena stifled, breath cut \'97 the \'b671 \'e9crasement's quieter sibling]\cf0 \strokec2 .\
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
